    "chapter": "3D Geometry",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (b)</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Line 1 passes through $\\vec{a}_1 = (1, -1, 1)$ with direction $\\vec{b}_1 = (2, 3, 4)$.<br/>Line 2 passes through $\\vec{a}_2 = (3, k, 0)$ with direction $\\vec{b}_2 = (1, 2, 1)$.<br/>If the lines intersect, they must be coplanar. Thus, $(\\vec{a}_2 - \\vec{a}_1) \\cdot (\\vec{b}_1 \\times \\vec{b}_2) = 0$.<br/>$\\vec{a}_2 - \\vec{a}_1 = (2, k+1, -1)$.<br/>Determinant:<br/>$|\\begin{matrix} 2 & k+1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\end{matrix}| = 0$<br/>$2(3 - 8) - (k+1)(2 - 4) - 1(4 - 3) = 0$<br/>$2(-5) - (k+1)(-2) - 1(1) = 0$<br/>$-10 + 2k + 2 - 1 = 0 \\implies 2k - 9 = 0 \\implies k = 9/2$.</p>",
