    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "A variable plane at a distance of 1 unit from the origin cuts the co-ordinate axes at $A,B$ and $C$ . If the centroid $D(x,y,z)$ of triangle $ABC$ satisfies the relation $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} + \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} + \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}} =k$ , then the value of $k$ is",
    "images": [],
