    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (a)</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The distance of $P(1,-2,1)$ from plane $x+2y-2z=\\alpha$ is 5.<br/>Distance formula: $d = \\frac{|1(1) + 2(-2) - 2(1) - \\alpha|}{\\sqrt{1^2 + 2^2 + (-2)^2}} = \\frac{|1-4-2-\\alpha|}{3} = \\frac{|-5-\\alpha|}{3}$.<br/>Since $\\alpha > 0$, $|-5-\\alpha| = \\alpha + 5$. So $\\frac{\\alpha + 5}{3} = 5 \\implies \\alpha = 10$.<br/>Equation of plane: $x + 2y - 2z = 10$.<br/>Let the foot of the perpendicular be $(x_1, y_1, z_1)$.<br/>Formula: $\\frac{x_1-1}{1} = \\frac{y_1+2}{2} = \\frac{z_1-1}{-2} = \\frac{-(1(1) + 2(-2) - 2(1) - 10)}{1^2 + 2^2 + (-2)^2} = \\frac{-(-15)}{9} = \\frac{5}{3}$.<br/>$x_1 = 1 + \\frac{5}{3} = \\frac{8}{3}$.<br/>$y_1 = -2 + \\frac{10}{3} = \\frac{4}{3}$.<br/>$z_1 = 1 - \\frac{10}{3} = -\\frac{7}{3}$.<br/>The foot of the perpendicular is $(\\frac{8}{3}, \\frac{4}{3}, -\\frac{7}{3})$.</p>",
