    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (b)</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $\\vec{u} = \\vec{AB} = 2\\hat{i} + 10\\hat{j} + 11\\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{v} = \\vec{AD} = -\\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + 2\\hat{k}$.<br/>$|\\vec{u}| = \\sqrt{4 + 100 + 121} = 15$. $|\\vec{v}| = \\sqrt{1 + 4 + 4} = 3$.<br/>$\\vec{u} \\cdot \\vec{v} = 2(-1) + 10(2) + 11(2) = 40$.<br/>Angle $\\theta$ between them: $\\cos \\theta = \\frac{40}{15 \\times 3} = \\frac{8}{9}$.<br/>Since $\\cos \\theta > 0$, $\\theta$ is acute.<br/>$AD$ is rotated by an acute angle $\\alpha$ in the plane to form $AD'$ such that $AD' \\perp AB$.<br/>This means the new angle is $90^\\circ$. So $\\theta + \\alpha = 90^\\circ$.<br/>$\\cos \\alpha = \\cos(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\sin \\theta = \\sqrt{1 - \\cos^2 \\theta} = \\sqrt{1 - 64/81} = \\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{9}$.</p>",
