    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (d)</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Line $L$: $x = 2r - 2, y = -r - 1, z = 3r$.<br/>General point on $L$ is $A(2r-2, -r-1, 3r)$.<br/>Foot of perpendicular $F$ from $A$ to plane $x+y+z=3$ is $(x,y,z)$.<br/>Since $AF \\perp$ plane, $F = (2r-2+t, -r-1+t, 3r+t)$.<br/>$F$ lies on plane: $(2r-2+t) + (-r-1+t) + (3r+t) = 3 \\implies 4r - 3 + 3t = 3 \\implies t = 2 - \\frac{4r}{3}$.<br/>Substitute $t$ into $F$:<br/>$x = 2r - 2 + 2 - \\frac{4r}{3} = \\frac{2r}{3}$<br/>$y = -r - 1 + 2 - \\frac{4r}{3} = 1 - \\frac{7r}{3}$<br/>$z = 3r + 2 - \\frac{4r}{3} = 2 + \\frac{5r}{3}$<br/>Let $\\lambda = \\frac{r}{3}$. Then $x = 2\\lambda, y = 1 - 7\\lambda, z = 2 + 5\\lambda$.<br/>Eliminating $\\lambda$: $\\frac{x}{2} = \\frac{y-1}{-7} = \\frac{z-2}{5}$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Hard"
