    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (c)</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The required plane is perpendicular to planes $2x+y-2z=5$ and $3x-6y-2z=7$.<br/>The normal vector $\\vec{n}$ to the required plane is the cross product of the normals of the given planes.<br/>$\\vec{n} = (2, 1, -2) \\times (3, -6, -2) = (-2 - 12, -6 - (-4), -12 - 3) = (-14, -2, -15)$.<br/>We can use $(14, 2, 15)$ as the normal vector.<br/>The plane passes through the point $(1, 1, 1)$.<br/>Equation: $14(x-1) + 2(y-1) + 15(z-1) = 0 \\implies 14x + 2y + 15z = 31$.</p>",
