    "text": "Consider the lines ${L}_{1}: \\frac{x-1}{2} = \\frac{y}{-1} = \\frac{z+3}{1}$ , ${L}_{2}: \\frac{x-4}{1} = \\frac{y+3}{1} = \\frac{z+3}{2}$ and the planes ${P}_{1}:7x+y+2z=3,{P}_{2}:3x+5y-6z=4$ . Let $ax+by+cz=d$ be the equation of the plane passing through the point of intersection of lines ${L}_{1}$ and ${L}_{2}$ and perpendicular to planes ${P}_{1}$ and ${P}_{2}$ . Match List-I with List-II and select the correct answer using the code given below the lists: List-I List-II (P) $a=$ (1) 13 (Q) $b=$ (2) -3 (R) $c=$ (3) 1 (S) $d=$ (4) -2 $P$$Q$$R$$S$",
