    "solution": "<p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>To find the unit vector perpendicular to both $L_1$ and $L_2$, we take the cross product of their direction vectors.<br/>Let the direction vector of $L_1$ be $\\vec{b}_1$ and that of $L_2$ be $\\vec{b}_2$.<br/>The normal vector is $\\vec{n} = \\vec{b}_1 \\times \\vec{b}_2$.<br/>The required unit vector is $\\hat{n} = \\pm \\frac{\\vec{b}_1 \\times \\vec{b}_2}{|\\vec{b}_1 \\times \\vec{b}_2|}$.<br/>Since the passage text is not fully present, evaluating this formula directly on the passage data gives the correct option.</p>",
