    "topic": "(Read The Passage Given Below And Answer The Questions That Follow)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Since the lines $L_1$ and $L_2$ are not provided in the text, we outline the general method.<br/>Let the direction vectors of $L_1$ and $L_2$ be $\\vec{b}_1$ and $\\vec{b}_2$.<br/>The plane's normal $\\vec{n}$ is perpendicular to both, so $\\vec{n} = \\vec{b}_1 \\times \\vec{b}_2$.<br/>The plane passes through $A(-1,-2,-1)$, so its equation is $\\vec{n} \\cdot (\\vec{r} - \\vec{a}) = 0$.<br/>Once the Cartesian equation $ax+by+cz+d=0$ is formed, the distance from $P(1,1,1)$ is found using $D = \\frac{|a(1) + b(1) + c(1) + d|}{\\sqrt{a^2+b^2+c^2}}$.<br/>Using the missing passage parameters would yield the correct option.</p>",
