    "type": "single mcq",
    "text": "Consider three planes ${P}_{1}:x-y+z=1$ ${P}_{2}:x+y-z=-1 {P}_{3}:x-3y+3z=2$ . Let ${L}_{1},{L}_{2},{L}_{3}$ be the lines of intersection of the planes ${P}_{2}$ and ${P}_{3},{P}_{3}$ and ${P}_{1}$ and ${P}_{1}$ and ${P}_{2}$ , respectively. Statement - 1: At least two of the lines ${L}_{1},{L}_{2}$ and ${L}_{3}$ are non-parallel. Statement - 2: The three planes do not have a common point.",
