    "type": "single mcq",
    "text": "Let $a,b,c$ be non zero real numbers such that $\\int\\limits_{0}^{1} \\left( 1+{cos}^{8}x \\right) \\left( a{x}^{2}+bx+c \\right) dx= \\int\\limits_{0}^{2} \\left( 1+{cos}^{8}x \\right) \\left( a{x}^{2}+bx+c \\right) dx$ Then the quadratic equation $a{x}^{2}+bx+c=0$ has",
    "images": [],
