    "chapter": "Application Of Calculus",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The slope of the normal to the curve $y=f(x)$ at the point $(3,4)$ is given by $m_n = \\tan(3\\pi/4) = -1$.<br/>We know that the slope of the tangent $m_t$ to the curve at the same point is the derivative evaluated at that point, i.e., $m_t = f\\'(3)$.<br/>Since the tangent and normal are perpendicular to each other, the product of their slopes is $-1$.<br/>$m_t \\cdot m_n = -1 \\implies f\\'(3) \\cdot (-1) = -1$<br/>$f\\'(3) = 1$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
