    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The curve is $y = (1-x)^2$. The total area lies between $x=0$ and $x=1$.<br/>The area $R_1$ is given by the integral from $0$ to $b$:<br/>$R_1 = \\int_0^b (1-x)^2 dx = \\left[ -\\frac{(1-x)^3}{3} \\right]_0^b = \\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{(1-b)^3}{3}$.<br/>The area $R_2$ is given by the integral from $b$ to $1$:<br/>$R_2 = \\int_b^1 (1-x)^2 dx = \\left[ -\\frac{(1-x)^3}{3} \\right]_b^1 = 0 - \\left(-\\frac{(1-b)^3}{3}\\right) = \\frac{(1-b)^3}{3}$.<br/>We are given that $R_1 - R_2 = \\frac{1}{4}$.<br/>Substitute $R_1$ and $R_2$ into the equation:<br/>$\\left( \\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{(1-b)^3}{3} \\right) - \\frac{(1-b)^3}{3} = \\frac{1}{4}$<br/>$\\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{2(1-b)^3}{3} = \\frac{1}{4}$<br/>$\\frac{2(1-b)^3}{3} = \\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{12}$<br/>$(1-b)^3 = \\frac{1}{12} \\times \\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{1}{8}$.<br/>Taking the cube root of both sides gives:<br/>$1 - b = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies b = \\frac{1}{2}$.</p>",
