    "text": "Let $f:[-1,2]\\rightarrow [0,\\infty )$ be a continuous function such that $f(x)=f(1-x)$ for all $x\\in [-1,2]$ . Let ${R}_{1}={∫}_{-1}^{2} xf(x)dx$ , and ${R}_{2}$ be the area of the region bounded by $y=f(x)$ , $x=-1,x=2$ , and the $x$ -axis. Then",
