    "type": "single mcq",
    "text": "If $f:R\\rightarrow R$ is a twice differentiable function such that ${f}^{''}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in R$ , and $f \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) = \\frac{1}{2} ,f(1)=1$ , then",
    "images": [],
