    "text": "If $y={f}^{'}(x)$ is a cubic polynomial having maxima at $x=-1$ and ${f}^{'}(x)$ has minima at $x=1$ , also $f(-1)=10$ , $f(1)=-6$ . Find the cubic polynomial and also find the distance between the points, which are maxima or minima.",
