    "type": "single mcq",
    "text": "If the function ${e}^{-x}f(x)$ assumes its minimum in the interval $[0,1]$ at $x=1/4$ , which of the following is true? (a) ${f}^{'}(x)<f(x), \\frac{1}{4} <x< \\frac{3}{4}$ (b) ${f}^{'}(x)>f(x),0<x< \\frac{1}{4}$ (c) ${f}^{'}(x)<f(x),0<x< \\frac{1}{4}$ (d) ${f}^{'}(x)<f(x), \\frac{3}{4} <x<1$",
    "images": [],
