    "id": "jee_adv_math_application_of_calculus_169",
    "number": "169",
    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "Let $f$ be a function defined on $R$ (the set of all real numbers) such that ${f}^{'}(x)=2010(x-2009)(x-2010{)}^{2}$ $(x-2011{)}^{3}(x-2012{)}^{4}$ , for all $x\\in R$ . If $g$ is a function defined on $R$ with values in the interval $(0,\\infty )$ such that $f(x)=ln(g(x))$ , for all $x\\in R$ , then the number of points in $R$ at which $g$ has a local maximum is",
