    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We need the coefficient of $t^{24}$ in the expansion of $(1 + t^2)^{12} (1 + t^{12}) (1 + t^{24})$.<br/>Expand $(1 + t^{12}) (1 + t^{24}) = 1 + t^{12} + t^{24} + t^{36}$.<br/>So the expression is $(1 + t^2)^{12} (1 + t^{12} + t^{24} + t^{36})$.<br/>The general term in the expansion of $(1 + t^2)^{12}$ is $\\binom{12}{r} t^{2r}$.<br/>To get $t^{24}$, we multiply terms from $(1 + t^2)^{12}$ with terms from $(1 + t^{12} + t^{24} + t^{36})$ such that their exponents sum to 24:<br/>Case 1: $t^{24}$ from $(1 + t^2)^{12}$ and $1$ from the second bracket.<br/>$2r = 24 \\implies r = 12$. Coefficient = $\\binom{12}{12} \\times 1 = 1 \\times 1 = 1$.<br/>Case 2: $t^{12}$ from $(1 + t^2)^{12}$ and $t^{12}$ from the second bracket.<br/>$2r = 12 \\implies r = 6$. Coefficient = $\\binom{12}{6} \\times 1 = 924 \\times 1 = 924$.<br/>Case 3: $t^0$ from $(1 + t^2)^{12}$ and $t^{24}$ from the second bracket.<br/>$2r = 0 \\implies r = 0$. Coefficient = $\\binom{12}{0} \\times 1 = 1 \\times 1 = 1$.<br/>The total coefficient of $t^{24}$ is the sum of these coefficients:<br/>Total = $1 + 924 + 1 = 926$.</p>",
