    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions\n (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We are given $A_r = \\binom{10}{r}$, $B_r = \\binom{20}{r}$, and $C_r = \\binom{30}{r}$.<br/>We need to evaluate $\\sum_{r=1}^{10} A_r (B_{10} B_r - C_{10} A_r) = B_{10} \\sum_{r=1}^{10} A_r B_r - C_{10} \\sum_{r=1}^{10} A_r^2$.<br/>Using Vandermonde\\'s identity:<br/>$\\sum_{r=0}^{10} A_r B_r = \\sum_{r=0}^{10} \\binom{10}{r} \\binom{20}{r} = \\sum_{r=0}^{10} \\binom{10}{10-r} \\binom{20}{r} = \\binom{30}{10} = C_{10}$.<br/>$\\sum_{r=0}^{10} A_r^2 = \\sum_{r=0}^{10} \\binom{10}{r}^2 = \\sum_{r=0}^{10} \\binom{10}{10-r} \\binom{10}{r} = \\binom{20}{10} = B_{10}$.<br/>Since the summation index in the problem starts from $r=1$, we subtract the $r=0$ term:<br/>$\\sum_{r=1}^{10} A_r B_r = C_{10} - A_0 B_0 = C_{10} - 1$.<br/>$\\sum_{r=1}^{10} A_r^2 = B_{10} - A_0^2 = B_{10} - 1$.<br/>Substitute these back into the expression:<br/>$= B_{10} (C_{10} - 1) - C_{10} (B_{10} - 1)$<br/>$= B_{10} C_{10} - B_{10} - C_{10} B_{10} + C_{10} = C_{10} - B_{10}$.</p>",
