    "correct": "-1",
    "chapter": "Binomial Theorem",
    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: -1</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>To find the sum of the coefficients of any polynomial $P(x)$, we simply substitute $x = 1$ into the polynomial expression.<br/>Let $P(x) = (1 + x - 3x^2)^{2163}$.<br/>Sum of coefficients = $P(1) = (1 + 1 - 3(1)^2)^{2163}$.<br/>$= (2 - 3)^{2163} = (-1)^{2163}$.<br/>Since $2163$ is an odd number, $(-1)^{2163} = -1$.<br/>Therefore, the sum of the coefficients is -1.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
