    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 2, 4</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We are given the binomial expansion $(1 + ax)^n = 1 + n(ax) + \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}(ax)^2 + \\dots$<br/>This must be identical to the given series $1 + 8x + 24x^2 + \\dots$<br/>By comparing the coefficients of $x$ and $x^2$:<br/>1) $na = 8$<br/>2) $\\frac{n(n-1)}{2} a^2 = 24$<br/>From the first equation, we get $a = \\frac{8}{n}$. Substitute this into the second equation:<br/>$\\frac{n(n-1)}{2} \\left(\\frac{8}{n}\\right)^2 = 24$<br/>$\\frac{n(n-1)}{2} \\frac{64}{n^2} = 24$<br/>$\\frac{32(n-1)}{n} = 24$<br/>$32n - 32 = 24n$<br/>$8n = 32 \\implies n = 4$.<br/>Substitute $n = 4$ back into the first equation:<br/>$4a = 8 \\implies a = 2$.<br/>So, $a = 2$ and $n = 4$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Easy"
