    "topic": "Match The Following",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>From the given paragraph:<br/>$C_1$: centre $O_1(0,0)$, radius $r_1=3$.<br/>$C_2$: centre $O_2(3,4)$, radius $r_2=4$.<br/>$C_3$ touches $C_1$ and $C_2$ such that they both lie inside $C_3$. Also, the centres are collinear.<br/>The diameter of $C_3$ is the distance between the farthest points of $C_1$ and $C_2$ on the line of centres.<br/>Distance $O_1O_2 = 5$. Diameter $= r_1 + O_1O_2 + r_2 = 3 + 5 + 4 = 12$.<br/>So, the radius of $C_3$ is $r=6$.<br/>The centre $O_3(h, k)$ is the midpoint of the farthest points $M$ and $N$.<br/>$M$ is on the opposite side of $O_2$ from $O_1$: $M = O_1 - r_1\\left(\\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{4}{5}\\right) = \\left(-\\frac{9}{5}, -\\frac{12}{5}\\right)$.<br/>$N$ is on the opposite side of $O_1$ from $O_2$: $N = O_2 + r_2\\left(\\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{4}{5}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{27}{5}, \\frac{36}{5}\\right)$.<br/>Midpoint $O_3$ is $\\left(\\frac{9}{5}, \\frac{12}{5}\\right)$. Thus $h=9/5, k=12/5$.<br/>(I) $2h+k = 2(9/5) + 12/5 = 6 \\implies$ (P).<br/>(II) Common chord $XY$ is $3x+4y-9=0$. Length $XY = 24/5$. Length of $ZW = 24\\sqrt{6}/5$. Ratio = $\\sqrt{6} \\implies$ (Q).<br/>(III) Area ratio of $\\Delta MZN$ to $\\Delta ZMW = 5/4 \\implies$ (R).<br/>(IV) Tangent to $C_1$ at $M$ is $3x+4y+15=0 \\implies y = -\\frac{3}{4}x - \\frac{15}{4}$. Tangency to $x^2=8\\alpha y \\implies -15/4 = -2\\alpha(-3/4)^2 \\implies \\alpha=10/3 \\implies$ (U).<br/>Matches: (I)-(P), (II)-(Q), (III)-(R), (IV)-(U). Based on the options provided, the correct option is selected.</p>",
