    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Since $\\omega$ is a complex cube root of unity, we know that $1 + \\omega + \\omega^2 = 0$ and $\\omega^3 = 1$.<br/>From this, $1 + \\omega = -\\omega^2$.<br/>Now, consider $(1 + \\omega)^7 = (-\\omega^2)^7 = -\\omega^{14}$.<br/>Since $\\omega^3 = 1$, we can write $\\omega^{14} = (\\omega^3)^4 \\cdot \\omega^2 = (1)^4 \\cdot \\omega^2 = \\omega^2$.<br/>Thus, $(1 + \\omega)^7 = -\\omega^2 = 1 + \\omega$.<br/>We are given $(1 + \\omega)^7 = A + B\\omega$.<br/>So, $1 + \\omega = A + B\\omega$.<br/>By comparing coefficients, we get $A = 1$ and $B = 1$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Medium"
