    "chapter": "Complex Number",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $\\omega = r e^{i\\theta}$. Then $|\\omega| = r$ and $\\text{Arg}(\\omega) = \\theta$.<br/>We are given $|z| = |\\omega|$, so $|z| = r$.<br/>We are also given $\\text{Arg}(z) + \\text{Arg}(\\omega) = \\pi \\implies \\text{Arg}(z) = \\pi - \\theta$.<br/>Therefore, $z = r e^{i(\\pi - \\theta)} = r e^{i\\pi} e^{-i\\theta}$.<br/>Since $e^{i\\pi} = -1$, we have $z = -r e^{-i\\theta}$.<br/>Also, $\\overline{\\omega} = r e^{-i\\theta}$.<br/>Substituting this back gives $z = -\\overline{\\omega}$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Easy"
