    "correct": "b",
    "chapter": "Complex Number",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $S = \\sum_{n=1}^{13} (i^n + i^{n+1})$.<br/>We can factor out $i^n$ from each term:<br/>$i^n + i^{n+1} = i^n(1 + i)$.<br/>So, $S = \\sum_{n=1}^{13} i^n(1 + i) = (1 + i) \\sum_{n=1}^{13} i^n$.<br/>The sum of any 4 consecutive powers of $i$ is zero ($i + i^2 + i^3 + i^4 = i - 1 - i + 1 = 0$).<br/>The sum of the first 12 terms is zero (3 groups of 4).<br/>$\\sum_{n=1}^{13} i^n = 0 + i^{13}$.<br/>Since $13 = 4 \\times 3 + 1$, $i^{13} = i^1 = i$.<br/>Therefore, $S = (1 + i)(i) = i + i^2 = i - 1$.</p>",
