    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $w_0 = \\frac{\\omega - \\overline{\\omega}z}{1 - z}$.<br/>Since $w_0$ is purely real, $w_0 = \\overline{w_0}$.<br/>$\\frac{\\omega - \\overline{\\omega}z}{1 - z} = \\frac{\\overline{\\omega} - \\omega\\overline{z}}{1 - \\overline{z}}$<br/>Cross-multiplying:<br/>$(\\omega - \\overline{\\omega}z)(1 - \\overline{z}) = (\\overline{\\omega} - \\omega\\overline{z})(1 - z)$<br/>$\\omega - \\omega\\overline{z} - \\overline{\\omega}z + \\overline{\\omega}z\\overline{z} = \\overline{\\omega} - \\overline{\\omega}z - \\omega\\overline{z} + \\omega z\\overline{z}$<br/>Cancel $-\\omega\\overline{z} - \\overline{\\omega}z$ from both sides:<br/>$\\omega + \\overline{\\omega}|z|^2 = \\overline{\\omega} + \\omega|z|^2$<br/>$\\omega - \\overline{\\omega} = \\omega|z|^2 - \\overline{\\omega}|z|^2 = (\\omega - \\overline{\\omega})|z|^2$.<br/>We are given $\\omega = \\alpha + i\\beta$ with $\\beta \\neq 0$, which means $\\omega \\neq \\overline{\\omega}$.<br/>So we can divide by $(\\omega - \\overline{\\omega})$:<br/>$1 = |z|^2 \\implies |z| = 1$.<br/>Therefore, the set of values of $z$ forms a circle of radius 1 centered at the origin (excluding $z=1$).</p>",
