    "text": "A particle $P$ starts from the point ${z}_{0}=1+2i$ , where $i= \\sqrt{-1}$ . It moves first horizontally away from origin by 5 units and then vertically away from origin by 3 units to reach a point ${z}_{1}$ . From ${z}_{1}$ the particle moves $\\sqrt{2}$ units in the direction of the vector $\\vec{i} + \\vec{j}$ and then it moves through an angle $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ in anticlockwise direction on a circle with centre at origin, to reach a point ${z}_{2}$ . The point ${z}_{2}$ is given by",
