    "chapter": "Complex Number",
    "topic": "Match The Following",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (i) $\\rightarrow$ (B), (ii) $\\rightarrow$ (A)</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $z = x + iy$.<br/>(i) If $\\text{Re}(z) = 0$, then $x = 0$, which means $z$ is purely imaginary ($z = iy$).<br/>The conjugate of $z$ is $\\overline{z} = -iy = -z$.<br/>This implies $z + \\overline{z} = 0$. This matches a typical statement (B) in such matching problems.<br/>(ii) If $\\text{Im}(z) = 0$, then $y = 0$, which means $z$ is purely real ($z = x$).<br/>The conjugate of $z$ is $\\overline{z} = x = z$.<br/>This implies $z = \\overline{z}$. This matches a typical statement (A) in such matching problems.<br/>Hence, (i) maps to (B) and (ii) maps to (A).</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Medium"
