    "chapter": "Complex Number",
    "topic": "(Read The Passage Given Below And Answer The Questions That Follow)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The expression $|z| - |\\omega| + 3$ depends on the distance from the origin to $z \\in A \\cap B \\cap C$ and the distance from the origin to $\\omega$, where $|\\omega - (2 + i)| < 3$.<br/>Finding the extremes of $|z|$ and $|\\omega|$ yields the bounds $-3$ and $9$. Thus, it lies between $-3$ and $9$, which is option (d).</p>",
