    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The region $S = S_1 \\cap S_2 \\cap S_3$ is defined by:<br/>$S_1$: $|z| < 4$ (interior of a circle of radius 4)<br/>$S_2$: $\\text{Im}\\left(\\frac{z - 1 + i\\sqrt{3}}{1 - i\\sqrt{3}}\\right) > 0$ (a half-plane)<br/>$S_3$: $\\text{Re}(z) > 0$ (the right half-plane)<br/>The intersection of these regions forms a sector of the circle. Calculating the angle of the sector and using the area formula $\\frac{1}{2}r^2\\theta$ yields the area corresponding to option (b).</p>",
