    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We are given $I_1 = \\int_{1-k}^k x f(x(1 - x)) dx$ and $I_2 = \\int_{1-k}^k f(x(1 - x)) dx$.<br/>Use the definite integral property $\\int_a^b h(x) dx = \\int_a^b h(a + b - x) dx$.<br/>Here, $a + b = (1 - k) + k = 1$.<br/>Substitute $x = 1 - x$ into $I_1$:<br/>$I_1 = \\int_{1-k}^k (1 - x) f((1 - x)(1 - (1 - x))) dx = \\int_{1-k}^k (1 - x) f((1 - x)x) dx$.<br/>$I_1 = \\int_{1-k}^k f(x(1 - x)) dx - \\int_{1-k}^k x f(x(1 - x)) dx$.<br/>This is exactly $I_1 = I_2 - I_1$.<br/>$2I_1 = I_2 \\implies \\frac{I_1}{I_2} = \\frac{1}{2}$.<br/>Thus, the ratio is $1/2$.</p>",
