    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $\\int_0^x f(t) dt = x + \\int_x^1 t f(t) dt$.<br/>Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$ using Leibniz\\'s Rule:<br/>$f(x) \\cdot 1 - f(0) \\cdot 0 = 1 + (0 - x f(x) \\cdot 1)$<br/>$f(x) = 1 - x f(x)$.<br/>Rearranging the terms:<br/>$f(x) + x f(x) = 1 \\implies f(x)(1 + x) = 1 \\implies f(x) = \\frac{1}{1 + x}$.<br/>We need to find the value of $f(1)$:<br/>$f(1) = \\frac{1}{1 + 1} = \\frac{1}{2}$.</p>",
