    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 2/5 (or 0.4)</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We are given $\\int_0^{t^2} x f(x) dx = \\frac{2}{5} t^5$.<br/>Differentiate both sides with respect to $t$ using Leibniz\\'s rule:<br/>$t^2 f(t^2) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dt}(t^2) = \\frac{2}{5} \\cdot 5t^4$.<br/>$t^2 f(t^2) \\cdot 2t = 2t^4$.<br/>$2t^3 f(t^2) = 2t^4$.<br/>Assuming $t \\neq 0$, we can divide by $2t^3$:<br/>$f(t^2) = t$.<br/>We need to find $f\\left(\\frac{4}{25}\\right)$. Let $t^2 = \\frac{4}{25}$.<br/>Since $t > 0$ (from context of principal root), $t = \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{25}} = \\frac{2}{5}$.<br/>Thus, $f\\left(\\frac{4}{25}\\right) = \\frac{2}{5} = 0.4$.</p>",
