    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a, b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $f(x) = 7\\tan^8 x + 7\\tan^6 x - 3\\tan^4 x - 3\\tan^2 x$.<br/>Factor the expression:<br/>$f(x) = 7\\tan^6 x (\\tan^2 x + 1) - 3\\tan^2 x (\\tan^2 x + 1)$.<br/>Since $\\tan^2 x + 1 = \\sec^2 x$:<br/>$f(x) = (7\\tan^6 x - 3\\tan^2 x)\\sec^2 x$.<br/>To integrate $f(x)$, let $t = \\tan x$, so $dt = \\sec^2 x dx$.<br/>$\\int f(x) dx = \\int (7t^6 - 3t^2) dt = t^7 - t^3 + C = \\tan^7 x - \\tan^3 x + C$.<br/>The correct expressions correspond to this integral evaluation.</p>",
