    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given the equation of a circle $x^2 + y^2 = 1$.<br/>Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$:<br/>$2x + 2y \\frac{dy}{dx} = 0 \\implies x + y \\frac{dy}{dx} = 0$.<br/>Differentiate again with respect to $x$ using the product rule on $y \\frac{dy}{dx}$:<br/>$1 + \\left( \\frac{dy}{dx} \\right)^2 + y \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = 0$.<br/>This differential equation represents the given family of curves and matches option (b).</p>",
