    "chapter": "Differential Equations",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The given differential equation is $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{\\sqrt{1-y^2}}{y}$.<br/>Separate the variables:<br/>$\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-y^2}} dy = dx$.<br/>Integrate both sides:<br/>$\\int \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-y^2}} dy = \\int dx$.<br/>Let $1-y^2 = t$, then $-2y dy = dt \\implies y dy = -dt/2$.<br/>$\\int \\frac{-dt/2}{\\sqrt{t}} = -\\sqrt{t} = -\\sqrt{1-y^2}$.<br/>So, $-\\sqrt{1-y^2} = x - C$.<br/>Square both sides:<br/>$1 - y^2 = (x - C)^2 \\implies (x - C)^2 + y^2 = 1$.<br/>This equation represents a family of circles whose centers are $(C, 0)$ and radii are equal to 1.<br/>Thus, the family consists of circles with centers on the x-axis and a fixed radius of 1.</p>",
