    "chapter": "Differential Equations",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The given equation is $8\\sqrt{x}(\\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}) dy = (\\sqrt{4+\\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}})^{-1} dx$.<br/>Rearranging gives $dy = \\frac{dx}{8\\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}\\sqrt{4+\\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}}}$.<br/>Let $t = \\sqrt{4+\\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}}$.<br/>Squaring gives $t^2 = 4 + \\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}$.<br/>Differentiating: $2t dt = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} dx = \\frac{dx}{4\\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}}$.<br/>So, $\\frac{dx}{8\\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}} = \\frac{t}{2} dt$.<br/>Substitute this into the expression for $dy$:<br/>$dy = \\frac{t/2}{t} dt = \\frac{1}{2} dt$.<br/>Integrate: $y = \\frac{1}{2} t + C = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{4+\\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}} + C$.<br/>Given $y(0) = \\sqrt{7}$:<br/>$\\sqrt{7} = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{4+\\sqrt{9}} + C = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{7} + C \\implies C = \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}$.<br/>So $y(x) = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{4+\\sqrt{9+\\sqrt{x}}} + \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}$.<br/>For $x = 256$:<br/>$\\sqrt{x} = 16$. $\\sqrt{9+16} = \\sqrt{25} = 5$. $\\sqrt{4+5} = 3$.<br/>$y(256) = \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}$.</p>",
