    "text": "Let $f:[1,\\infty )\\rightarrow R$ be a differentiable function such that $f(1)= \\frac{1}{3}$ and $3{∫}_{1}^{x} f(t)dt=xf(x)- \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3} ,x\\in [1,\\infty )$ Let $e$ denote the base of the natural logarithm. Then the value of $f(e)$ is",
