    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "Let $f(x)$ be a continuously differentiable function on the interval $(0,\\infty )$ such that $f(1)=2$ and ${lim}_{t\\rightarrow x} \\frac{{t}^{10}f(x)-{x}^{10}f(t)}{{t}^{9}-{x}^{9}} =1$ for each $x>0$ . Then, for all $x>0,f(x)$ is equal to",
    "images": [],
