    "chapter": "Differential Equations",
    "topic": "(With One Or More Than One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b, c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $f\\'(x) = e^{f(x)-g(x)} g\\'(x)$.<br/>Rewrite as $f\\'(x) e^{-f(x)} = g\\'(x) e^{-g(x)}$.<br/>Integrate both sides with respect to $x$:<br/>$\\int f\\'(x) e^{-f(x)} dx = \\int g\\'(x) e^{-g(x)} dx$.<br/>$-e^{-f(x)} = -e^{-g(x)} + C \\implies e^{-g(x)} - e^{-f(x)} = C$.<br/>This relation defines the properties that match options (b) and (c).</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
