    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The equation is $y\\' + 12y = \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{12}\\right)$.<br/>The integrating factor is $IF = e^{12x}$.<br/>$y e^{12x} = \\int e^{12x} \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{12}\\right) dx$.<br/>Using the formula $\\int e^{ax} \\cos(bx) dx = \\frac{e^{ax}}{a^2+b^2} (a\\cos bx + b\\sin bx)$ with $a=12, b=\\pi/12$:<br/>$y e^{12x} = \\frac{e^{12x}}{144 + \\pi^2/144} \\left( 12\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{12}\\right) + \\frac{\\pi}{12}\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{12}\\right) \\right) + C$.<br/>$y(x) = \\frac{144}{144^2 + \\pi^2} \\left( 12\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{12}\\right) + \\frac{\\pi}{12}\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{12}\\right) \\right) + C e^{-12x}$.<br/>Applying $y(0) = 0$ finds $C$. Evaluate the function to check the given options.</p>",
