    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "Let $f$ be a real-valued differentiable function on $R$ (the set of all real numbers) such that $f(1)=1$ . If the $y$ -intercept of the tangent at any point $P(x,y)$ on the curve $y=f(x)$ is equal to the cube of the abscissa of $P$ , then the value of $f(-3)$ is equal to____________",
