    "topic": "Numerical/Integer Value Type Questions",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 6</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The full question based on the typical JEE Advanced problem is: \"Let $f:[1,\\infty )\\rightarrow [2,\\infty )$ be a differentiable function such that $f(1)=2$. If $6\\int_1^x f(t)dt = 3xf(x) - x^3$ for all $x \\ge 1$, then the value of $f(2)$ is\".<br/>Given $6 \\int_1^x f(t) dt = 3x f(x) - x^3$.<br/>Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$ using Leibniz\\'s rule:<br/>$6 f(x) = 3 f(x) + 3x f\\'(x) - 3x^2$.<br/>Rearrange the terms:<br/>$3x f\\'(x) - 3f(x) = 3x^2 \\implies x f\\'(x) - f(x) = x^2 \\implies f\\'(x) - \\frac{1}{x} f(x) = x$.<br/>This is a linear differential equation. The integrating factor is:<br/>$IF = e^{\\int -\\frac{1}{x} dx} = e^{-\\ln x} = \\frac{1}{x}$.<br/>Multiply by the IF:<br/>$\\frac{d}{dx} \\left( f(x) \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = 1$.<br/>Integrate both sides:<br/>$\\frac{f(x)}{x} = x + C \\implies f(x) = x^2 + Cx$.<br/>Given $f(1) = 2$:<br/>$2 = 1^2 + C(1) \\implies C = 1$.<br/>So $f(x) = x^2 + x$.<br/>We need to find $f(2)$:<br/>$f(2) = 2^2 + 2 = 4 + 2 = 6$.</p>",
