    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The given function is $f(x) = \\begin{vmatrix} x^3 & \\sin x & \\cos x \\\\ 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ p & p^2 & p^3 \\end{vmatrix}$.<br/>Expand the determinant along the first row:<br/>$f(x) = x^3(-1 \\cdot p^3 - 0 \\cdot p^2) - \\sin x(6 \\cdot p^3 - 0 \\cdot p) + \\cos x(6 \\cdot p^2 - (-1)p)$.<br/>$f(x) = -p^3 x^3 - 6p^3 \\sin x + (6p^2 + p) \\cos x$.<br/>Now find the third derivative $\\frac{d^3}{dx^3}(f(x))$:<br/>$f\\'(x) = -3p^3 x^2 - 6p^3 \\cos x - (6p^2 + p) \\sin x$.<br/>$f\\'\\'(x) = -6p^3 x + 6p^3 \\sin x - (6p^2 + p) \\cos x$.<br/>$f\\'\\'\\'(x) = -6p^3 + 6p^3 \\cos x + (6p^2 + p) \\sin x$.<br/>Evaluate at $x = 0$:<br/>$f\\'\\'\\'(0) = -6p^3 + 6p^3(1) + (6p^2 + p)(0) = -6p^3 + 6p^3 = 0$.<br/>Thus, the value is 0, which corresponds to option (d).</p>",
