    "chapter": "Differentiation",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $x \\cos y + y \\cos x = \\pi$.<br/>Find $y$ at $x = 0$: $0 \\cdot \\cos y + y \\cos 0 = \\pi \\implies y(1) = \\pi \\implies y = \\pi$.<br/>Differentiate implicitly with respect to $x$:<br/>$\\cos y - x \\sin y \\cdot y\\' + y\\' \\cos x - y \\sin x = 0$.<br/>Substitute $x = 0$ and $y = \\pi$ to find $y\\'(0)$:<br/>$\\cos \\pi - 0 + y\\'(0) \\cos 0 - \\pi \\sin 0 = 0 \\implies -1 + y\\'(0)(1) = 0 \\implies y\\'(0) = 1$.<br/>Differentiate again with respect to $x$:<br/>$-\\sin y \\cdot y\\' - \\left( \\sin y \\cdot y\\' + x \\cos y \\cdot (y\\')^2 + x \\sin y \\cdot y\\'\\' \\right) + y\\'\\' \\cos x - y\\' \\sin x - (y\\' \\sin x + y \\cos x) = 0$.<br/>$-2\\sin y \\cdot y\\' - x\\cos y \\cdot (y\\')^2 - x\\sin y \\cdot y\\'\\' + y\\'\\'\\cos x - 2y\\'\\sin x - y\\cos x = 0$.<br/>Substitute $x = 0, y = \\pi, y\\' = 1$:<br/>$-2\\sin \\pi (1) - 0 - 0 + y\\'\\'(0) \\cos 0 - 2(1)\\sin 0 - \\pi \\cos 0 = 0$.<br/>$0 + y\\'\\'(0)(1) - \\pi(1) = 0 \\implies y\\'\\'(0) = \\pi$.<br/>This corresponds to option (b).</p>",
