    "text": "If $y= \\frac{a{x}^{2}}{(x-a)(x-b)(x-c)} + \\frac{bx}{(x-b)(x-c)} + \\frac{x}{(x-c)} +1$ , prove that $\\frac{{y}^{'}}{y} = \\frac{1}{x} \\left( \\frac{a}{a-x} + \\frac{b}{b-x} + \\frac{c}{c-x} \\right)$",
