    "type": "fill_in_the_blanks",
    "text": "If $f(x)=|x-2|$ and $g(x)=f(f(x))$ then ${g}^{'}(x)=$ $$ for $x>20$",
    "images": [],
    "options": [],
    "correct": "1",
    "chapter": "Differentiation",
    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 1</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $f(x) = |x - 2|$ and $g(x) = f(f(x))$.<br/>For $x > 20$, $x - 2$ is positive, so $f(x) = x - 2$.<br/>Then $g(x) = f(x - 2) = |(x - 2) - 2| = |x - 4|$.<br/>For $x > 20$, $x - 4$ is positive, so $g(x) = x - 4$.<br/>Differentiating with respect to $x$:<br/>$g\\'(x) = \\frac{d}{dx}(x - 4) = 1$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Hard"
