    "number": "9",
    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "The ellipse ${E}_{1}: \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} + \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} =1$ is inscribed in a rectangle $R$ whose sides are parallel to the coordinate axes. Another ellipse ${E}_{2}$ passing through the point $(0,4)$ circumscribes the rectangle $R$ . The eccentricity of the ellipse ${E}_{2}$ is",
