    "type": "subjective",
    "text": "Let $P$ be a point on the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}} + \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} =1,0<b<a$ . Let the line parallel to $y$ -axis, passing through $P$ meets the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={a}^{2}$ at the point $Q$ such that $P$ and $Q$ are on the same side of $x$ -axis. For two positive real numbers $r$ and $s$ , find the locus of the point $R$ on $PQ$ such that $PR$ : $RQ=r:s$ and $P$ varies over the ellipse.",
