    "correct": "c",
    "chapter": "Ellipse",
    "topic": "Match The Following",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The vertices of $\\triangle PAB$ are $P(3,4)$, $A(3,0)$, and $B\\left(-\\frac{9}{5}, \\frac{8}{5}\\right)$.<br/>Since $P$ and $A$ have the same x-coordinate, the line $PA$ is vertical ($x = 3$).<br/>The altitude from $B$ to $PA$ must be a horizontal line passing through $B$, which is $y = \\frac{8}{5}$.<br/>The slope of $PB$ is $\\frac{4 - 8/5}{3 - (-9/5)} = \\frac{12/5}{24/5} = \\frac{1}{2}$.<br/>The altitude from $A$ to $PB$ has a slope of $-2$. Its equation is $y - 0 = -2(x - 3) \\implies y = -2x + 6$.<br/>The orthocentre $H$ is the intersection of these two altitudes:<br/>Substitute $y = \\frac{8}{5}$ into $y = -2x + 6$:<br/>$\\frac{8}{5} = -2x + 6 \\implies 2x = 6 - \\frac{8}{5} = \\frac{22}{5} \\implies x = \\frac{11}{5}$.<br/>The orthocentre is $\\left(\\frac{11}{5}, \\frac{8}{5}\\right)$, which matches option c.</p>",
