    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "Suppose that the foci of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} + \\frac{{y}^{2}}{5} =1$ are $\\left( {f}_{1},0 \\right)$ and $\\left( {f}_{2},0 \\right)$ where ${f}_{1}>0$ and ${f}_{2}<0$ . Let ${P}_{1}$ and ${P}_{2}$ be two parabolas with a common vertex at $(0,0)$ and with foci at $\\left( {f}_{1},0 \\right)$ and $\\left( 2{f}_{2},0 \\right)$ respectively. Let ${T}_{1}$ be a tangent to ${P}_{1}$ which passes through $\\left( 2{f}_{2},0 \\right)$ and ${T}_{2}$ be a tangent to ${P}_{2}$ which passes through $\\left( {f}_{1},0 \\right)$ . If ${m}_{1}$ is the slope of ${T}_{1}$ and ${m}_{2}$ is the slope of ${T}_{2}$ , then the value of $\\left( \\frac{1}{{m}_{1}^{2}} +{m}_{2}^{2} \\right)$ is",
