    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $f(x) = (x+1)^2 - 1$ for $x \\ge -1$.<br/>In this domain, $f(x)$ is strictly increasing.<br/>For a strictly increasing function, the points where $f(x) = f^{-1}(x)$ are exactly the points where $f(x) = x$.<br/>Setting $f(x) = x$:<br/>$(x+1)^2 - 1 = x \\implies x^2 + 2x + 1 - 1 = x \\implies x^2 + x = 0$<br/>$x(x + 1) = 0 \\implies x = 0$ or $x = -1$.<br/>Both of these values satisfy the condition $x \\ge -1$.<br/>So the set is $\\{0, -1\\}$.</p>",
