    "topic": "True/False",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: True</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $f(x) = (a - x^n)^{1/n}$.<br/>We want to evaluate $f(f(x))$.<br/>$f(f(x)) = \\left( a - (f(x))^n \\right)^{1/n}$.<br/>Substitute $f(x)$:<br/>$f(f(x)) = \\left( a - \\left( (a - x^n)^{1/n} \\right)^n \\right)^{1/n}$.<br/>The power $1/n$ and $n$ cancel out:<br/>$f(f(x)) = \\left( a - (a - x^n) \\right)^{1/n} = (x^n)^{1/n} = x$.<br/>So $f(f(x)) = x$ is a true statement.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
