    "correct": "\\frac{-3x}{2} + \\frac{35}{36}\\log (9e^{2x} - 4) + C",
    "chapter": "Indefinite Integrals",
    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: \\frac{-3x}{2} + \\frac{35}{36}\\log (9e^{2x} - 4) + C</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $I = \\int \\frac{4e^{2x} + 6}{9e^{2x} - 4} dx$.<br/>We express the numerator as a linear combination of the denominator and its derivative:<br/>$4e^{2x} + 6 = A(9e^{2x} - 4) + B\\frac{d}{dx}(9e^{2x} - 4)$<br/>$4e^{2x} + 6 = A(9e^{2x} - 4) + B(18e^{2x}) = (9A + 18B)e^{2x} - 4A$.<br/>Comparing coefficients:<br/>Constant term: $-4A = 6 \\implies A = -3/2$.<br/>$e^{2x}$ coefficient: $9A + 18B = 4 \\implies 9(-3/2) + 18B = 4 \\implies -27/2 + 18B = 4 \\implies 18B = 35/2 \\implies B = 35/36$.<br/>Now substitute this into the integral:<br/>$I = \\int \\frac{-\\frac{3}{2}(9e^{2x} - 4) + \\frac{35}{36}(18e^{2x})}{9e^{2x} - 4} dx$<br/>$I = -\\frac{3}{2} \\int 1 dx + \\frac{35}{36} \\int \\frac{18e^{2x}}{9e^{2x} - 4} dx$.<br/>$I = -\\frac{3}{2}x + \\frac{35}{36}\\log|9e^{2x} - 4| + C$.<br/>This matches the given answer.</p>",
