    "number": "5",
    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "If ${sin}^{-1} \\left( x- \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} + \\frac{{x}^{3}}{4} ….. \\right)$ $+{cos}^{-1} \\left( {x}^{2}- \\frac{{x}^{4}}{2} + \\frac{{x}^{6}}{4} -…… \\right) = \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ for $0<|x|< \\sqrt{2}$ , then $x$ equals",
    "images": [],
