    "number": "4",
    "type": "single mcq",
    "text": "The function $f(x)= \\frac{ln(1+ax)-ln(1-bx)}{x}$ is not defined at $x=0$ . The value which should be assigned to $f$ at $x=0$ so that it is continuous at $x=0$ , is",
