    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The function is $f(x) = [\\tan^2 x]$.<br/>As $x \\to 0$, we know that $\\tan x \\to 0$.<br/>Because $\\tan^2 x \\ge 0$ for all $x$, and for values of $x$ very close to 0, $0 \\le \\tan^2 x < 1$.<br/>Therefore, the greatest integer $[\\tan^2 x] = 0$ for all $x$ in a small neighborhood around 0.<br/>This means $f(x) = 0$ in this neighborhood.<br/>The limit as $x \\to 0$ of $f(x)$ is $0$, and the function value at $x=0$ is $f(0) = [0] = 0$.<br/>Since $\\lim_{x \\to 0} f(x) = f(0)$, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$.<br/>Matches option b.</p>",
