    "number": "43",
    "type": "multiple mcq",
    "text": "Let $g(x)$ be a function defined on $(-1,1)$ . If the area of the equilateral triangle with two of its vertices at $(0,0)$ and $(x,g(x))$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}$ then the function $g(x)$ is,",
