    "number": "100",
    "type": "subjective",
    "text": "Let $f(x)= \\left( \\begin{bmatrix} x+a & if & x<0 \\\\ |x-1| & if & x\\geq 0 \\end{bmatrix} \\right)$ and $g(x)= \\left( \\begin{bmatrix} x+1 & if & x<0 \\\\ (x-1{)}^{2}+b & if & x\\geq 0 \\end{bmatrix} \\right)$ , where $a$ and $b$ are non-negative real numbers. Determine the composite function $gof$ . If $(gof)(x)$ is continuous for all real $x$ , determine the values of $a$ and $b$ . Further, for these values of $a$ and $b$ , is gof differentiable at $x=0$ ? Justify your answer.",
