    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 1</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We need to find $\\lim_{x \\to 0} g(f(x))$.<br/>For $x \\to 0$ (but $x \\neq 0$), $f(x) = \\sin x$.<br/>As $x \\to 0$, $f(x) = \\sin x \\to 0$.<br/>Also, for $x$ close to 0 but $x \\neq 0$, $f(x) = \\sin x \\neq 0$.<br/>Therefore, the limit becomes $\\lim_{y \\to 0, y \\neq 0} g(y)$.<br/>For $y \\neq 0, 2$, $g(y) = y^2 + 1$.<br/>$\\lim_{y \\to 0} (y^2 + 1) = 0^2 + 1 = 1$.<br/>Thus, $\\lim_{x \\to 0} g(f(x)) = 1$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Easy"
