    "id": "jee_adv_math_limits_continuity_and_differentiability_131",
    "number": "131",
    "type": "single mcq",
    "text": "Let $f$ and $g$ be real valued functions defined on interval $(-1,1)$ such that ${g}^{''}(x)$ is continuous, $g(0)\\neq 0,{g}^{'}(0)=0$ , ${g}^{''}(0)\\neq 0$ and $f(x)=g(x)sinx$ . Statement - 1: ${lim}_{x\\rightarrow \\infty } [g(x)cotx-g(0)cosecx]={f}^{''}(0)$ . Statement - 2: ${f}^{'}(0)=g(0)$ .",
    "images": [],
