    "number": "136",
    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "Let $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$ be such that ${lim}_{x\\rightarrow 0} \\frac{{x}^{2}sin(\\beta x)}{\\alpha x-sinx} =1$ . Then $6(\\alpha +\\beta )$ equals",
    "images": [],
