    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $X = \\frac{x^2}{a^2}, Y = \\frac{y^2}{b^2}, Z = \\frac{z^2}{c^2}$.<br/>The system of equations becomes:<br/>$X + Y - Z = 1$<br/>$X - Y + Z = 1$<br/>$-X + Y + Z = 1$<br/>Adding the first and second equations gives: $2X = 2 \\implies X = 1$.<br/>Adding the second and third equations gives: $2Z = 2 \\implies Z = 1$.<br/>Adding the first and third equations gives: $2Y = 2 \\implies Y = 1$.<br/>Since $X=1, Y=1, Z=1$, we have:<br/>$\\frac{x^2}{a^2} = 1 \\implies x = \\pm a$<br/>$\\frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1 \\implies y = \\pm b$<br/>$\\frac{z^2}{c^2} = 1 \\implies z = \\pm c$<br/>Since $a,b,c$ are real numbers, there are $2 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 8$ solutions for $(x, y, z)$.<br/>Since there is a finite number of solutions (8), the system has finitely many solutions.</p>",
