    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $\\Delta = \\begin{vmatrix} 6i & -3i & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3i & -1 \\\\ 20 & 3 & i \\end{vmatrix}$.<br/>Expand the determinant along the first row:<br/>$= 6i (3i \\cdot i - (-1) \\cdot 3) - (-3i) (4 \\cdot i - (-1) \\cdot 20) + 1 (4 \\cdot 3 - 3i \\cdot 20)$<br/>$= 6i (3i^2 + 3) + 3i (4i + 20) + 1 (12 - 60i)$<br/>Since $i^2 = -1$, $3i^2 + 3 = -3 + 3 = 0$.<br/>So the first term is 0.<br/>The second term is $3i(4i + 20) = 12i^2 + 60i = -12 + 60i$.<br/>The third term is $12 - 60i$.<br/>Adding them together:<br/>$\\Delta = 0 + (-12 + 60i) + (12 - 60i) = 0$.<br/>Thus, $\\Delta = 0 + 0i$.<br/>Comparing with $x + iy$, we get $x = 0$ and $y = 0$.</p>",
