    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The given homogeneous system of equations is:<br/>$1x + ay + 0z = 0$<br/>$0x + 1y + az = 0$<br/>$ax + 0y + 1z = 0$<br/>For the system to have infinitely many solutions, the determinant of the coefficient matrix must be zero.<br/>$D = \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & a \\\\ a & 0 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} = 0$.<br/>Expanding the determinant along the first row:<br/>$1(1 \\times 1 - a \\times 0) - a(0 \\times 1 - a \\times a) + 0 = 0$<br/>$1 - a(-a^2) = 0 \\implies 1 + a^3 = 0$.<br/>$\\implies a^3 = -1 \\implies a = -1$ (since $a$ must be real).<br/>Thus, $a = -1$.</p>",
