    "text": "Let $ω\\neq 1$ be a cube root of unity and $S$ be the set of all non-singular matrices of the form $\\left( \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & a & b \\\\ ω & 1 & c \\\\ {ω}^{2} & ω & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\right)$ , where each of $a,b$ and $c$ is either $ω$ or ${ω}^{2}$ . Then the number of distinct matrices in the set $S$ is",
