    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We are given $P^T = 2P + I$.<br/>Taking the transpose of both sides, we get:<br/>$(P^T)^T = (2P + I)^T \\implies P = 2P^T + I^T = 2P^T + I$.<br/>Now, substitute $P^T = 2P + I$ into this equation:<br/>$P = 2(2P + I) + I$<br/>$P = 4P + 2I + I$<br/>$P = 4P + 3I$<br/>$-3P = 3I \\implies P = -I$.<br/>Thus, $P$ is the negative of the identity matrix.<br/>We need to find the relation for $PX$.<br/>$PX = (-I)X = -X$.</p>",
