    "id": "jee_adv_math_matrices_and_determinants_71",
    "number": "71",
    "type": "fill_in_the_blanks",
    "text": "For positive numbers $x,y$ and $z$ , the numerical value of the determinant $\\left( \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & {log}_{x}y & {log}_{x}z \\\\ {log}_{y}x & 1 & {log}_{y}z \\\\ {log}_{z}x & {log}_{z}y & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\right)$ is",
    "images": [],
    "options": [],
    "correct": "0",
    "chapter": "Matrices And Determinants",
    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 0</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Using the change of base formula, $\\log_x y = \\frac{\\ln y}{\\ln x}$.<br/>Let $\\ln x = A, \\ln y = B, \\ln z = C$.<br/>The determinant becomes:<br/>$D = \\begin{vmatrix} A/A & B/A & C/A \\\\ A/B & B/B & C/B \\\\ A/C & B/C & C/C \\end{vmatrix}$.<br/>Factor out $1/A$ from the first row, $1/B$ from the second, and $1/C$ from the third:<br/>$D = \\frac{1}{ABC} \\begin{vmatrix} A & B & C \\\\ A & B & C \\\\ A & B & C \\end{vmatrix}$.<br/>Since all three rows are identical, the value of the determinant is $0$.</p>",
