    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We are given $C_1: y^2 = 4x$ and $C_2: x^2 + y^2 - 6x + 1 = 0$.<br/>Substitute $y^2 = 4x$ into the equation of $C_2$:<br/>$x^2 + 4x - 6x + 1 = 0 \\implies x^2 - 2x + 1 = 0 \\implies (x-1)^2 = 0$.<br/>This gives a repeated root $x = 1$.<br/>Since $x=1$ is a repeated root, the curves are tangent (touch each other) at the intersection points.<br/>For $x = 1$, $y^2 = 4(1) \\implies y = \\pm 2$.<br/>The points of intersection are $(1, 2)$ and $(1, -2)$.<br/>Thus, $C_1$ and $C_2$ touch each other exactly at two points.</p>",
