    "topic": "(With One Or More Than One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a, d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>For $P(at^2, 2at)$ on $y^2 = 4ax$, the tangent is $ty = x + at^2$, which meets the axis ($y=0$) at $T(-at^2, 0)$.<br/>The normal is $y = -tx + 2at + at^3$, which meets the axis at $N(2a+at^2, 0)$.<br/>The centroid $G(h,k)$ of $\\triangle PTN$ is given by:<br/>$h = \\frac{-at^2 + (2a+at^2) + at^2}{3} = \\frac{2a + at^2}{3}$.<br/>$k = \\frac{0 + 0 + 2at}{3} = \\frac{2at}{3} \\implies t = \\frac{3k}{2a}$.<br/>Substitute $t$ into the equation for $h$:<br/>$h = \\frac{2a + a(\\frac{9k^2}{4a^2})}{3} = \\frac{2a}{3} + \\frac{3k^2}{4a}$.<br/>$\\frac{3k^2}{4a} = h - \\frac{2a}{3} \\implies k^2 = \\frac{4a}{3} \\left(h - \\frac{2a}{3}\\right)$.<br/>The locus is a parabola $y^2 = \\frac{4a}{3}\\left(x - \\frac{2a}{3}\\right)$.<br/>Its vertex is $(2a/3, 0)$.<br/>The focal length parameter $A$ is given by $4A = 4a/3 \\implies A = a/3$.<br/>Focus = $(\\frac{2a}{3} + \\frac{a}{3}, 0) = (a, 0)$.<br/>Thus, options (a) and (d) are correct.</p>",
