    "correct": "c, d",
    "chapter": "Parabola",
    "topic": "(With One Or More Than One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c, d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $A(t_1^2, 2t_1)$ and $B(t_2^2, 2t_2)$ be points on $y^2 = 4x$ (where $a=1$).<br/>The circle with diameter $AB$ has its center at the midpoint of $AB$, which is $C\\left(\\frac{t_1^2+t_2^2}{2}, t_1+t_2\\right)$.<br/>The circle touches the axis of the parabola (the x-axis). The radius $r$ is the perpendicular distance from the center to the x-axis, so $r = |t_1 + t_2|$.<br/>The slope of the line joining $A$ and $B$ is $m = \\frac{2t_2 - 2t_1}{t_2^2 - t_1^2} = \\frac{2}{t_1 + t_2}$.<br/>Since $|t_1 + t_2| = r$, we have $t_1 + t_2 = \\pm r$.<br/>Thus, the slope $m = \\frac{2}{\\pm r} = \\pm \\frac{2}{r}$.<br/>Options (c) and (d) are correct.</p>",
