    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a, c, d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The circle is $x^2 + y^2 - 4x - 16y + 64 = 0$ with center $S(2, 8)$ and radius $R = \\sqrt{4+64-64} = 2$.<br/>The point $P$ on $y^2 = 4x$ closest to $S$ lies on the normal to the parabola passing through $S$.<br/>Normal to $y^2=4x$ is $y = -tx + 2t + t^3$. Since it passes through $(2,8)$, we have $8 = -2t + 2t + t^3 \\implies t^3 = 8 \\implies t = 2$.<br/>Thus, $P = (t^2, 2t) = (4, 4)$.<br/>Distance $SP = \\sqrt{(4-2)^2 + (4-8)^2} = \\sqrt{4+16} = 2\\sqrt{5}$. (Option a is correct)<br/>$Q$ is on the circle and on $SP$, so $SQ = R = 2$.<br/>$QP = SP - SQ = 2\\sqrt{5} - 2$.<br/>Ratio $SQ : QP = 2 : (2\\sqrt{5} - 2) = 1 : (\\sqrt{5}-1) = (\\sqrt{5}+1) : 4$. (Option b is false)<br/>The normal at $P$ is $2x + y = 12$. Its x-intercept ($y=0$) is $x=6$. (Option c is correct)<br/>The tangent to the circle at $Q$ is perpendicular to the radius $SQ$ (which lies along $SP$).<br/>Slope of $SP = \\frac{8-4}{2-4} = -2$.<br/>Thus, slope of the tangent at $Q = 1/2$. (Option d is correct).</p>",
