    "chapter": "Parabola",
    "topic": "(With One Or More Than One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a, b, d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The parabola is $E: y^2 = 8x$, so $a = 2$. Focus $F$ is $(2, 0)$.<br/>The point $P(-2, 4)$ has an x-coordinate of -2, which means it lies on the directrix $x = -2$.<br/>By the properties of a parabola, tangents drawn from any point on the directrix are perpendicular to each other. Therefore, $\\angle QPQ' = 90^\\circ$, and $\\triangle QPQ'$ is a right-angled triangle. (Option b is true).<br/>Also, the chord of contact $QQ'$ for a point on the directrix passes through the focus $F$. Thus, $F$ lies on $QQ'$. (Option d is true).<br/>The segment of a tangent between the point of contact and the directrix subtends a right angle at the focus. Thus $\\angle PFQ = 90^\\circ$, making $\\triangle PFQ$ right-angled. (Option a is true).<br/>Distance $PF = \\sqrt{(-2-2)^2 + (4-0)^2} = \\sqrt{16+16} = 4\\sqrt{2} \\neq 5\\sqrt{2}$. (Option c is false).</p>",
