    "chapter": "Parabola",
    "topic": "(With One Or More Than One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b, c, d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The parabola is $y^2=4x \\implies a=1, S(1,0)$.<br/>For $P(-2,1)$, the chord of contact is $y(1) = 2(x-2) \\implies 2x - y - 4 = 0$.<br/>Solving with $y^2 = 4x$ gives points $P_1(4,4)$ and $P_2(1,-2)$.<br/>The line $SP_1$ has slope $\\frac{4-0}{4-1} = \\frac{4}{3}$, giving $4x - 3y - 4 = 0$.<br/>The line $SP_2$ is the vertical line $x=1$.<br/>$Q_2$ is the foot of the perpendicular from $P(-2,1)$ to $x=1$, which is $Q_2(1,1)$.<br/>$SQ_2 = \\sqrt{(1-1)^2 + (1-0)^2} = 1$. (Option d is true).<br/>The line $PQ_1 \\perp SP_1$ passes through $P(-2,1)$ with slope $-3/4$. Equation: $3x + 4y + 2 = 0$.<br/>$Q_1$ is the intersection of $4x - 3y = 4$ and $3x + 4y = -2$, which is $Q_1(2/5, -4/5)$.<br/>$PQ_1$ distance is $\\frac{|4(-2) - 3(1) - 4|}{\\sqrt{16+9}} = \\frac{|-15|}{5} = 3$. (Option c is true).<br/>$SQ_1 = \\sqrt{(2/5-1)^2 + (-4/5-0)^2} = \\sqrt{9/25 + 16/25} = 1 \\neq 2$. (Option a is false).<br/>$Q_1 Q_2 = \\sqrt{(1 - 2/5)^2 + (1 - (-4/5))^2} = \\sqrt{(3/5)^2 + (9/5)^2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{90}}{5} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{5}$. (Option b is true).</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
