    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: x + y = 3</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>For the parabola $x^2 = 4y$, $a=1$. The parametric coordinates are $(2t, t^2)$.<br/>The equation of the normal at $t$ is $x + ty = 2t + t^3$.<br/>Since it passes through $(1, 2)$, we substitute $x=1, y=2$:<br/>$1 + 2t = 2t + t^3 \\implies t^3 = 1 \\implies t = 1$.<br/>Substitute $t=1$ into the normal equation:<br/>$x + y = 2(1) + 1^3 \\implies x + y = 3$.</p>",
