    "correct": "2 : 1",
    "chapter": "Parabola",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 2 : 1</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>This is a standard property of parabolas: The area of the triangle formed by any three points on a parabola is exactly twice the area of the triangle formed by the tangents at these three points.<br/>Therefore, the ratio of the areas of $\\Delta ABC$ (formed by points on the parabola) and $\\Delta PQR$ (formed by the intersections of their tangents) is $2 : 1$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Medium"
