    "correct": "c",
    "chapter": "Parabola",
    "topic": "Match The Following",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the circle $C_1$ have its center at the origin $O(0,0)$ and radius 1. Let $L$ be the given line.<br/>Let the moving circle have center $S$ and radius $r$.<br/>Since it touches $C_1$ externally, the distance $SO = r + 1$.<br/>Since it touches the line $L$, the distance from $S$ to $L$ is $r$.<br/>Since both circles are on the same side of $L$, we can write: distance $SO - \\text{distance from } S \\text{ to } L = 1$.<br/>This means that the distance from $S$ to the origin $O$ equals the distance from $S$ to a line $L'$ (which is parallel to $L$ and 1 unit further away from $O$).<br/>The locus of a point whose distance from a fixed point (origin) equals its distance to a fixed line ($L'$) is a parabola.<br/>Thus, the locus of $S$ is a parabola.</p>",
