    "topic": "Match The Following",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The circle $x^2+y^2=9$ and parabola $y^2=8x$ intersect where $x^2+8x-9=0 \\implies x=1$ (since $x>0$).<br/>So $y^2 = 8 \\implies y = \\pm 2\\sqrt{2}$. The points are $P(1, 2\\sqrt{2})$ and $Q(1, -2\\sqrt{2})$.<br/>Tangent to the circle at $P(1, 2\\sqrt{2})$ is $x + 2\\sqrt{2}y = 9$. It intersects the x-axis at $R(9,0)$.<br/>Tangent to the parabola at $P(1, 2\\sqrt{2})$ is $y(2\\sqrt{2}) = 4(x+1)$. It intersects the x-axis at $S(-1,0)$.<br/>The area of $\\Delta PQS$ is $\\frac{1}{2} \\times PQ \\times \\text{distance from } S \\text{ to } PQ = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4\\sqrt{2} \\times (1 - (-1)) = 4\\sqrt{2}$.<br/>The area of $\\Delta PQR$ is $\\frac{1}{2} \\times PQ \\times \\text{distance from } R \\text{ to } PQ = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4\\sqrt{2} \\times (9 - 1) = 16\\sqrt{2}$.<br/>Ratio of areas is $\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{16\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{1}{4} = 1:4$.</p>",
