    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The vertices of $\\Delta PRS$ are $P(1, 2\\sqrt{2})$, $R(9,0)$, and $S(-1,0)$.<br/>The sides are $RS = 9 - (-1) = 10$.<br/>$PR = \\sqrt{(9-1)^2 + (0-2\\sqrt{2})^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 8} = \\sqrt{72} = 6\\sqrt{2}$.<br/>$PS = \\sqrt{(-1-1)^2 + (0-2\\sqrt{2})^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 8} = \\sqrt{12} = 2\\sqrt{3}$.<br/>The area of $\\Delta PRS = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 2\\sqrt{2} = 10\\sqrt{2}$.<br/>The radius of the circumcircle is given by $R = \\frac{abc}{4A} = \\frac{10 \\times 6\\sqrt{2} \\times 2\\sqrt{3}}{4 \\times 10\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{120\\sqrt{6}}{40\\sqrt{2}} = 3\\sqrt{3}$.</p>",
