    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The vertices of $\\Delta PQR$ are $P(1, 2\\sqrt{2})$, $Q(1, -2\\sqrt{2})$, and $R(9,0)$.<br/>$PQ = 4\\sqrt{2}$. By symmetry, $PR = QR = \\sqrt{8^2 + (2\\sqrt{2})^2} = \\sqrt{72} = 6\\sqrt{2}$.<br/>The semiperimeter $s = \\frac{4\\sqrt{2} + 6\\sqrt{2} + 6\\sqrt{2}}{2} = 8\\sqrt{2}$.<br/>The area of $\\Delta PQR$ is $\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4\\sqrt{2} \\times 8 = 16\\sqrt{2}$.<br/>The radius of the incircle is $r = \\frac{A}{s} = \\frac{16\\sqrt{2}}{8\\sqrt{2}} = 2$.</p>",
