    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Tangents at the ends of a focal chord $PQ$ intersect on the directrix $x = -a$.<br/>They are given to meet on the line $y = 2x + a$.<br/>Substituting $x = -a$, we get $y = 2(-a) + a = -a$.<br/>So the point of intersection of tangents is $T(-a, -a)$.<br/>The chord of contact $PQ$ from $T$ is $y(-a) = 2a(x - a) \\implies -y = 2x - 2a \\implies y = -2x + 2a$.<br/>The slope of the focal chord $PQ$ is $\\tan \\theta = -2$.<br/>The length of a focal chord with angle $\\theta$ is $4a \\csc^2 \\theta = 4a (1 + \\cot^2 \\theta) = 4a(1 + 1/4) = 5a$.</p>",
