    "chapter": "Parabola",
    "topic": "Match The Following",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $P(at^2, 2at)$. Since $PQ$ is a focal chord, the parameter for $Q$ is $-1/t$.<br/>The point $K$ is $(2a, 0)$.<br/>Slope of $PK$ is $\\frac{2at - 0}{at^2 - 2a} = \\frac{2t}{t^2 - 2}$.<br/>The slope of $QR$ (with parameters $-1/t$ and $r$) is $\\frac{2}{r - 1/t} = \\frac{2t}{rt - 1}$.<br/>Since $PK \\parallel QR$, their slopes are equal:<br/>$\\frac{2t}{t^2 - 2} = \\frac{2t}{rt - 1} \\implies t^2 - 2 = rt - 1 \\implies rt = t^2 - 1 \\implies r = \\frac{t^2 - 1}{t} = t - 1/t$.</p>",
