    "correct": "\\frac{a",
    "chapter": "Parabola",
    "topic": "Match The Following",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The tangent at $P(at^2, 2at)$ is $ty = x + at^2$.<br/>The normal at $S(as^2, 2as)$ is $y = -sx + 2as + as^3$.<br/>Since $st = 1 \\implies s = 1/t$, the normal at $S$ is $y = -\\frac{1}{t}x + \\frac{2a}{t} + \\frac{a}{t^3} \\implies x + ty = 2a + \\frac{a}{t^2}$.<br/>We have the system:<br/>$x - ty = -at^2$<br/>$x + ty = 2a + a/t^2$<br/>Subtracting the first from the second gives $2ty = at^2 + 2a + a/t^2 = a(t^2 + 2 + 1/t^2) = a(t + 1/t)^2$.<br/>So $y = \\frac{a(t^2+1)^2}{2t^3}$.</p>",
