    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 2</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>For the parabola $y^2=8x$, $a=2$. The endpoints of the latus rectum are $L(2, 4)$ and $L'(2, -4)$.<br/>The area $\\Delta_1$ of the triangle formed by $P(1/2, 2)$, $L$, and $L'$ is:<br/>$\\Delta_1 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}$.<br/>The base $LL'$ lies on $x=2$ and has length $4 - (-4) = 8$.<br/>The height of $P(1/2, 2)$ from $x=2$ is $|2 - 1/2| = 3/2$.<br/>So $\\Delta_1 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 8 \\times \\frac{3}{2} = 6$.<br/>By the standard property of parabolas, the area of the triangle formed by tangents at any three points is half the area of the triangle formed by the points themselves.<br/>Therefore, $\\Delta_1 / \\Delta_2 = 2$.</p>",
