    "chapter": "Permutations And Combinations",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The given expression is $\\binom{n}{r} + 2\\binom{n}{r-1} + \\binom{n}{r-2}$.<br/>We can expand the middle term to rewrite the sum as:<br/>$= \\left[ \\binom{n}{r} + \\binom{n}{r-1} \\right] + \\left[ \\binom{n}{r-1} + \\binom{n}{r-2} \\right]$<br/>Using Pascal's identity, $\\binom{n}{k} + \\binom{n}{k-1} = \\binom{n+1}{k}$, we can simplify both brackets:<br/>$\\binom{n}{r} + \\binom{n}{r-1} = \\binom{n+1}{r}$<br/>$\\binom{n}{r-1} + \\binom{n}{r-2} = \\binom{n+1}{r-1}$<br/>Substituting these back into the expression, we get:<br/>$= \\binom{n+1}{r} + \\binom{n+1}{r-1}$<br/>Applying Pascal's identity one more time:<br/>$= \\binom{n+2}{r}$.<br/>This matches option c.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Easy"
