    "chapter": "Permutations And Combinations",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>A grid with sides $2m-1$ and $2n-1$ has $2m$ horizontal lines and $2n$ vertical lines.<br/>Let the horizontal lines be indexed $0, 1, 2, \\dots, 2m-1$ ($m$ even indices and $m$ odd indices).<br/>Let the vertical lines be indexed $0, 1, 2, \\dots, 2n-1$ ($n$ even indices and $n$ odd indices).<br/>A rectangle is formed by choosing 2 horizontal lines and 2 vertical lines.<br/>For the side length to be odd, the difference between the indices of the chosen lines must be odd.<br/>This implies we must choose one line with an even index and one line with an odd index.<br/>The number of ways to choose 2 horizontal lines with an odd difference is $m \\times m = m^2$.<br/>The number of ways to choose 2 vertical lines with an odd difference is $n \\times n = n^2$.<br/>Total number of such rectangles is $m^2 \\times n^2 = m^2 n^2$.</p>",
