    "chapter": "Permutations And Combinations",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The given series is $\\sum_{k=0}^{20} (-1)^k \\binom{30}{k} \\binom{30}{10+k}$.<br/>Since $\\binom{30}{10+k} = \\binom{30}{30 - (10+k)} = \\binom{30}{20-k}$, the series can be rewritten as:<br/>$\\sum_{k=0}^{20} (-1)^k \\binom{30}{k} \\binom{30}{20-k}$.<br/>This is exactly the coefficient of $x^{20}$ in the product of the expansions of $(1 - x)^{30}$ and $(1 + x)^{30}$.<br/>$(1 - x)^{30} (1 + x)^{30} = (1 - x^2)^{30}$.<br/>The general term in the expansion of $(1 - x^2)^{30}$ is $(-1)^r \\binom{30}{r} (x^2)^r = (-1)^r \\binom{30}{r} x^{2r}$.<br/>To find the coefficient of $x^{20}$, we set $2r = 20 \\implies r = 10$.<br/>The coefficient is $(-1)^{10} \\binom{30}{10} = \\binom{30}{10}$.</p>",
