    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $p = r^{a_1} t^{b_1} s^{c_1}$ and $q = r^{a_2} t^{b_2} s^{c_2}$.<br/>Their LCM is $r^{\\max(a_1, a_2)} t^{\\max(b_1, b_2)} s^{\\max(c_1, c_2)}$.<br/>We are given that the LCM is $r^2 t^4 s^2$.<br/>So, $\\max(a_1, a_2) = 2$. The possible pairs $(a_1, a_2)$ are $(0,2), (1,2), (2,2), (2,1), (2,0)$. There are $2(2) + 1 = 5$ pairs.<br/>$\\max(b_1, b_2) = 4$. The possible pairs $(b_1, b_2)$ are $2(4) + 1 = 9$ pairs.<br/>$\\max(c_1, c_2) = 2$. The possible pairs $(c_1, c_2)$ are $2(2) + 1 = 5$ pairs.<br/>The total number of ordered pairs $(p, q)$ is $5 \\times 9 \\times 5 = 225$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Medium"
