    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The word is COCHIN. The letters in alphabetical order are C, C, H, I, N, O.<br/>We need to find the number of words that appear before COCHIN in the dictionary.<br/>Since COCHIN starts with C, we consider words starting with C. The first letter is fixed as C.<br/>The remaining letters to be arranged are C, H, I, N, O (all distinct).<br/>The words starting with C and having their second letter alphabetically before O:<br/>- Starting with C C: The number of ways to arrange the remaining 4 letters is $4! = 24$.<br/>- Starting with C H: Number of ways is $4! = 24$.<br/>- Starting with C I: Number of ways is $4! = 24$.<br/>- Starting with C N: Number of ways is $4! = 24$.<br/>The next words start with C O. The first word starting with C O will have the remaining letters (C, H, I, N) in alphabetical order.<br/>Alphabetical order of C, H, I, N is C H I N.<br/>So the first word starting with C O is C O C H I N, which is our target word.<br/>Therefore, the total number of words before COCHIN is $24 + 24 + 24 + 24 = 96$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Easy"
