    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We need to form 7-digit numbers using 1, 2, 3 such that the sum of digits is 10.<br/>Let the base number be formed by seven 1's: $1+1+1+1+1+1+1 = 7$.<br/>We need to increase this sum by 3 (to get 10) by changing some 1's to 2's or 3's.<br/>Case 1: Change three 1's to 2's (each adds 1).<br/>The digits are 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2. Sum = 10.<br/>Number of arrangements = $\\frac{7!}{4! 3!} = 35$.<br/>Case 2: Change one 1 to a 2 (adds 1) and one 1 to a 3 (adds 2).<br/>The digits are 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 3. Sum = 10.<br/>Number of arrangements = $\\frac{7!}{5! 1! 1!} = 42$.<br/>Total number of integers = $35 + 42 = 77$.</p>",
