    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We need to distribute 5 distinct balls among 3 distinct persons such that each gets at least one.<br/>This is equivalent to finding the number of surjective (onto) functions from a set of 5 elements to a set of 3 elements.<br/>The formula is $3^5 - \\binom{3}{1}2^5 + \\binom{3}{2}1^5 - \\binom{3}{3}0^5$.<br/>$= 243 - 3(32) + 3(1)$<br/>$= 243 - 96 + 3 = 150$.<br/>Thus, there are 150 ways.</p>",
