    "chapter": "Permutations And Combinations",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The club has 6 girls and 4 boys. A team of 4 is to be selected with at most 1 boy, and a captain is to be chosen from the 4 selected members.<br/>Case 1: 0 boys and 4 girls.<br/>Number of ways to select the team = $\\binom{6}{4} = 15$.<br/>Number of ways to select the captain from the 4 members = 4.<br/>Total ways for Case 1 = $15 \\times 4 = 60$.<br/>Case 2: 1 boy and 3 girls.<br/>Number of ways to select the team = $\\binom{4}{1} \\times \\binom{6}{3} = 4 \\times 20 = 80$.<br/>Number of ways to select the captain from the 4 members = 4.<br/>Total ways for Case 2 = $80 \\times 4 = 320$.<br/>Total number of ways = $60 + 320 = 380$.</p>",
