    "type": "single mcq",
    "text": "Let $S{1,2,3,…,9}$ . For $k=1,2,…,5$ , let ${N}_{k}$ be the number of subsets of $S$ , each containing five elements out of which exactly $k$ are odd. Then ${N}_{1}+{N}_{2}+{N}_{3}+$ ${N}_{4}+{N}_{5}=$",
    "images": [],
