    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the foot of the perpendicular from $(x_1, y_1)$ on the line $ax + by + c = 0$ be $(x, y)$.<br/>The coordinates are given by the formula:<br/>$\\frac{x - x_1}{a} = \\frac{y - y_1}{b} = -\\frac{ax_1 + by_1 + c}{a^2 + b^2}$.<br/>Here, the point is $(2, 3)$ and the line is $3x - y + 4 = 0$.<br/>So $x_1 = 2, y_1 = 3, a = 3, b = -1, c = 4$.<br/>$\\frac{x - 2}{3} = \\frac{y - 3}{-1} = -\\frac{3(2) - 1(3) + 4}{3^2 + (-1)^2}$<br/>$= -\\frac{6 - 3 + 4}{10} = -\\frac{7}{10}$.<br/>Now, $x - 2 = 3(-\\frac{7}{10}) = -\\frac{21}{10} \\implies x = 2 - 2.1 = -0.1 = -\\frac{1}{10}$.<br/>$y - 3 = -1(-\\frac{7}{10}) = \\frac{7}{10} \\implies y = 3 + 0.7 = 3.7 = \\frac{37}{10}$.<br/>The foot of the perpendicular is $(-1/10, 37/10)$.</p>",
