    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The vertices of the triangle are formed by the intersections of the three lines: $x=0$ (y-axis), $y=0$ (x-axis), and $\\frac{x}{a} + \\frac{y}{b} = 1$.<br/>The intersections are $(0,0)$, $(a,0)$, and $(0,b)$.<br/>Since the sides lie on the coordinate axes, the triangle is a right-angled triangle with the right angle at the origin $(0,0)$.<br/>For a right-angled triangle, the circumcentre is the midpoint of the hypotenuse.<br/>The hypotenuse is the line segment joining $(a,0)$ and $(0,b)$.<br/>Midpoint $= \\left( \\frac{a+0}{2}, \\frac{0+b}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{a}{2}, \\frac{b}{2} \\right)$.</p>",
