    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the vertices be $A(0,0), B(3,4), C(4,0)$.<br/>The orthocentre is the intersection of the altitudes.<br/>Altitude from $B(3,4)$ to $AC$: $AC$ lies on the x-axis ($y=0$), so the altitude from $B$ is a vertical line passing through $B$. Equation: $x = 3$.<br/>Altitude from $A(0,0)$ to $BC$: Slope of $BC = \\frac{0-4}{4-3} = -4$.<br/>Slope of the altitude from $A = \\frac{-1}{-4} = \\frac{1}{4}$.<br/>Equation of the altitude from $A$: $y - 0 = \\frac{1}{4}(x - 0) \\implies y = \\frac{x}{4}$.<br/>To find the orthocentre, we solve the two altitude equations:<br/>$x = 3$ and $y = \\frac{x}{4}$.<br/>Substitute $x = 3 \\implies y = \\frac{3}{4}$.<br/>The orthocentre is $(3, 3/4)$.</p>",
