    "correct": "b",
    "chapter": "Points, Straight Lines And Family Of Straight Lines",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Triangle $PQR$ is right-angled isosceles at $P(2, 1)$.<br/>So, the angle at $P$ is $90^\\circ$ and the angles at $Q$ and $R$ are $45^\\circ$.<br/>This means the lines $PQ$ and $PR$ make an angle of $45^\\circ$ with the line $QR$.<br/>The equation of $QR$ is $2x + y = 3$, so its slope is $m = -2$.<br/>Let the slope of $PQ$ (or $PR$) be $m'$. The angle between them is $45^\\circ$, so:<br/>$\\tan 45^\\circ = \\left| \\frac{m' - (-2)}{1 + m'(-2)} \\right| \\implies 1 = \\left| \\frac{m' + 2}{1 - 2m'} \\right|$<br/>$1 - 2m' = m' + 2 \\implies 3m' = -1 \\implies m' = -1/3$<br/>or $1 - 2m' = -(m' + 2) \\implies 1 - 2m' = -m' - 2 \\implies m' = 3$.<br/>The slopes of $PQ$ and $PR$ are $3$ and $-1/3$.<br/>The equations of the lines through $P(2, 1)$ are:<br/>$y - 1 = 3(x - 2) \\implies 3x - y - 5 = 0$<br/>$y - 1 = -\\frac{1}{3}(x - 2) \\implies x + 3y - 5 = 0$<br/>The joint equation is $(3x - y - 5)(x + 3y - 5) = 0$.<br/>$3x^2 + 9xy - 15x - xy - 3y^2 + 5y - 5x - 15y + 25 = 0$<br/>$3x^2 - 3y^2 + 8xy - 20x - 10y + 25 = 0$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Medium"
