    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The vertices of the triangle are $P(2,2), Q(6,-1)$ and $R(7,3)$.<br/>$PS$ is the median, so $S$ is the midpoint of $QR$.<br/>Coordinates of $S = \\left( \\frac{6+7}{2}, \\frac{-1+3}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{13}{2}, 1 \\right)$.<br/>The slope of $PS = \\frac{1 - 2}{\\frac{13}{2} - 2} = \\frac{-1}{\\frac{9}{2}} = -\\frac{2}{9}$.<br/>We need the equation of a line parallel to $PS$ and passing through $(1, -1)$.<br/>Parallel line has the same slope, $m = -\\frac{2}{9}$.<br/>Equation: $y - (-1) = -\\frac{2}{9}(x - 1)$<br/>$9(y + 1) = -2(x - 1)$<br/>$9y + 9 = -2x + 2$<br/>$2x + 9y + 7 = 0$.</p>",
