    "chapter": "Points, Straight Lines And Family Of Straight Lines",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The equations of the lines are $3x + 4y = 9$ and $y = mx + 1$.<br/>Substitute $y$ in the first equation:<br/>$3x + 4(mx + 1) = 9$<br/>$3x + 4mx + 4 = 9$<br/>$x(3 + 4m) = 5 \\implies x = \\frac{5}{3 + 4m}$.<br/>For $x$ to be an integer, the denominator $3 + 4m$ must be a divisor of 5.<br/>The divisors of 5 are $1, -1, 5, -5$.<br/>Case 1: $3 + 4m = 1 \\implies 4m = -2 \\implies m = -1/2$ (Not an integer).<br/>Case 2: $3 + 4m = -1 \\implies 4m = -4 \\implies m = -1$ (Integer).<br/>Case 3: $3 + 4m = 5 \\implies 4m = 2 \\implies m = 1/2$ (Not an integer).<br/>Case 4: $3 + 4m = -5 \\implies 4m = -8 \\implies m = -2$ (Integer).<br/>Thus, the integer values for $m$ are $-1$ and $-2$.<br/>There are 2 such values.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Hard"
