    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The area of a parallelogram formed by lines $y = mx + c_1, y = mx + c_2$ and $y = nx + d_1, y = nx + d_2$ is given by the formula:<br/>Area $= \\frac{|(c_1 - c_2)(d_1 - d_2)|}{|m - n|}$.<br/>Here, the lines are $y = mx, y = mx+1$ (so $c_1=0, c_2=1$) and $y = nx, y = nx+1$ (so $d_1=0, d_2=1$).<br/>Substitute these values into the formula:<br/>Area $= \\frac{|(0 - 1)(0 - 1)|}{|m - n|} = \\frac{1}{|m - n|}$.</p>",
