    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The points are $P(-1,0), Q(0,0)$ and $R(3, 3\\sqrt{3})$.<br/>$Q$ is the origin. The line segment $QP$ lies along the negative x-axis, so its angle is $\\pi$.<br/>The point $R$ is in the first quadrant. Its angle $\\phi$ with the positive x-axis is given by $\\tan\\phi = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{3} = \\sqrt{3} \\implies \\phi = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$.<br/>The internal angle bisector of $\\angle PQR$ divides the angle between the rays $QP$ and $QR$ equally.<br/>The angle of the bisector with the positive x-axis will be $\\frac{\\pi + \\pi/3}{2} = \\frac{4\\pi/3}{2} = \\frac{2\\pi}{3}$.<br/>The slope of the bisector is $\\tan(2\\pi/3) = -\\sqrt{3}$.<br/>The equation of the bisector passing through the origin is $y = -\\sqrt{3}x$, which is $\\sqrt{3}x + y = 0$.</p>",
