    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the straight line through the origin be $y = mx$.<br/>It meets $L_1: 4x + 2y = 9$ at $P$ and $L_2: 2x + y = -6$ at $Q$.<br/>Note that $L_1$ and $L_2$ are parallel lines.<br/>The ratio in which the origin $O$ divides the segment $PQ$ is equal to the ratio of the perpendicular distances from $O$ to the two parallel lines.<br/>Distance from $O(0,0)$ to $4x + 2y - 9 = 0$ is $d_1 = \\frac{|-9|}{\\sqrt{4^2 + 2^2}} = \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{20}}$.<br/>Distance from $O(0,0)$ to $2x + y + 6 = 0$ is $d_2 = \\frac{|6|}{\\sqrt{2^2 + 1^2}} = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{12}{\\sqrt{20}}$.<br/>The ratio is $OP / OQ = d_1 / d_2 = \\frac{9/\\sqrt{20}}{12/\\sqrt{20}} = \\frac{9}{12} = \\frac{3}{4}$.</p>",
