    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The triangle is bounded by the axes $x=0, y=0$ and the line passing through $(0, 21)$ and $(21, 0)$, which is $x + y = 21$.<br/>The interior of the triangle is the region where $x > 0, y > 0$ and $x + y < 21$.<br/>We need to find the number of positive integer solutions $(x, y)$ to $x + y \\le 20$.<br/>For a fixed integer $x$ (where $1 \\le x \\le 19$), $y$ can take any integer value from $1$ to $20 - x$.<br/>The number of such points is $\\sum_{x=1}^{19} (20 - x) = 19 + 18 + \\dots + 1$.<br/>Sum = $\\frac{19 \\times 20}{2} = 190$.</p>",
