    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the vertices be $A(0,0), B(3,4)$ and $C(4,0)$.<br/>The side $AC$ lies on the x-axis, so the altitude from $B(3,4)$ is the vertical line $x = 3$.<br/>The slope of $BC$ is $\\frac{0 - 4}{4 - 3} = -4$.<br/>The altitude from $A(0,0)$ to $BC$ is a line through the origin with slope $\\frac{-1}{-4} = \\frac{1}{4}$.<br/>Its equation is $y = \\frac{1}{4}x$.<br/>The orthocentre is the intersection of these two altitudes: $x = 3$ and $y = \\frac{1}{4}x$.<br/>Substitute $x=3$ into the second equation: $y = \\frac{3}{4}$.<br/>The orthocentre is $(3, 3/4)$.</p>",
