    "chapter": "Points, Straight Lines And Family Of Straight Lines",
    "topic": "(With One Or More Than One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b, c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The circle is $x^2 + y^2 - x + 3y = 0$, which has center $C\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, -\\frac{3}{2}\\right)$ and radius $r = \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}$.<br/>If a circle makes equal intercepts on two lines, it means the center of the circle is equidistant from both lines.<br/>Line $L_2$ is $x + y - 1 = 0$.<br/>Distance from $C$ to $L_2$ is $d_2 = \\frac{|1/2 - 3/2 - 1|}{\\sqrt{1^2 + 1^2}} = \\frac{|-2|}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\sqrt{2}$.<br/>Let the line $L_1$ passing through the origin be $mx - y = 0$.<br/>Distance from $C$ to $L_1$ is $d_1 = \\frac{|m/2 - (-3/2)|}{\\sqrt{m^2 + 1}} = \\frac{|m + 3|}{2\\sqrt{m^2 + 1}}$.<br/>Set $d_1 = d_2$: $\\frac{|m + 3|}{2\\sqrt{m^2 + 1}} = \\sqrt{2}$.<br/>Squaring both sides: $\\frac{m^2 + 6m + 9}{4(m^2 + 1)} = 2 \\implies m^2 + 6m + 9 = 8m^2 + 8$.<br/>$7m^2 - 6m - 1 = 0 \\implies (7m + 1)(m - 1) = 0$.<br/>So $m = 1$ or $m = -1/7$.<br/>The equations of $L_1$ can be $y = x \\implies x - y = 0$ or $y = -\\frac{1}{7}x \\implies x + 7y = 0$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Easy"
