    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 7x - 4y + 25 = 0, 0.4x + 7y - 11 = 0, 0.7x - 4y - 3 = 0</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The side of the rectangle is on the line $L_1: 4x + 7y + 5 = 0$. Its slope is $-4/7$.<br/>We check the vertices $(-3, 1)$ and $(1, 1)$.<br/>For $(-3, 1)$: $4(-3) + 7(1) + 5 = 0$. Thus, $A(-3, 1)$ lies on $L_1$.<br/>For $(1, 1)$: $4(1) + 7(1) + 5 = 16 \\neq 0$. Thus, $C(1, 1)$ is the opposite vertex.<br/>The side $AB$ is perpendicular to $L_1$ and passes through $A(-3,1)$. Its slope is $7/4$.<br/>Equation of $AB$: $y - 1 = \\frac{7}{4}(x + 3) \\implies 7x - 4y + 25 = 0$.<br/>The side $CD$ is parallel to $AB$ and passes through $C(1,1)$. Its slope is $7/4$.<br/>Equation of $CD$: $y - 1 = \\frac{7}{4}(x - 1) \\implies 7x - 4y - 3 = 0$.<br/>The side $BC$ is parallel to $L_1$ and passes through $C(1,1)$. Its slope is $-4/7$.<br/>Equation of $BC$: $y - 1 = -\\frac{4}{7}(x - 1) \\implies 4x + 7y - 11 = 0$.<br/>These are the equations of the other three sides.</p>",
