    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (-a, a(t_1 + t_2 + t_3 + t_1 t_2 t_3))</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The given points are the vertices of a triangle formed by the tangents to the parabola $y^2 = 4ax$ at points corresponding to parameters $t_1, t_2, t_3$.<br/>The vertices of such a triangle are given precisely by the coordinates in the problem: $(at_1t_2, a(t_1+t_2))$, etc.<br/>A well-known property of parabolas states that the orthocentre of a triangle formed by any three tangents to a parabola lies on the directrix of the parabola.<br/>The directrix of $y^2 = 4ax$ is the line $x = -a$. So the x-coordinate of the orthocentre is $-a$.<br/>By calculating the equations of the altitudes and solving them, the y-coordinate of the orthocentre is found to be $y = a(t_1 + t_2 + t_3 + t_1 t_2 t_3)$.<br/>Hence, the orthocentre is $(-a, a(t_1 + t_2 + t_3 + t_1 t_2 t_3))$.</p>",
