    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: (a^2 + b^2)(lx + my + n) - 2(al + bm)(ax + by + c) = 0</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The line $L_1: ax+by+c=0$ bisects the angle between the lines $L_2: lx+my+n=0$ and the required line $L=0$.<br/>Thus, the perpendicular distance from any point on $L_1$ to $L_2$ is equal to its perpendicular distance to $L$.<br/>By reflecting $L_2$ across $L_1$, we can obtain the equation of $L$.<br/>Any line passing through the intersection $P$ of $L_1$ and $L_2$ can be written as $L_2 + \\lambda L_1 = 0$.<br/>By applying the angle condition or by finding the image of a point on $L_2$ under reflection in $L_1$, the specific value of $\\lambda$ can be deduced.<br/>The resulting equation of the reflected line $L$ simplifies to:<br/>$(a^2 + b^2)(lx + my + n) - 2(al + bm)(ax + by + c) = 0$.</p>",
