    "number": "63",
    "type": "subjective",
    "text": "A straight line $L$ with negative slopes passes through the point $(8,2)$ and cuts the positive coordinate axes at points $P$ and $Q$ . Find the absolute minimum value of $OP+OQ$ , as $L$ varies, where $O$ is the origin.",
    "images": [],
    "options": [],
    "correct": "18",
    "chapter": "Points, Straight Lines And Family Of Straight Lines",
    "topic": "Subjective Problems",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 18</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the line $L$ have slope $m < 0$. Since it passes through $(8, 2)$, its equation is $y - 2 = m(x - 8)$.<br/>The x-intercept $P$ is found by setting $y = 0 \\implies x_P = 8 - \\frac{2}{m}$.<br/>The y-intercept $Q$ is found by setting $x = 0 \\implies y_Q = 2 - 8m$.<br/>Since $m < 0$, let $m = -k$ where $k > 0$.<br/>Then $x_P = 8 + \\frac{2}{k}$ and $y_Q = 2 + 8k$.<br/>We want to minimize $OP + OQ = x_P + y_Q = (8 + \\frac{2}{k}) + (2 + 8k) = 10 + 8k + \\frac{2}{k}$.<br/>By AM-GM inequality, $8k + \\frac{2}{k} \\ge 2\\sqrt{8k \\cdot \\frac{2}{k}} = 2\\sqrt{16} = 8$.<br/>So, $OP + OQ \\ge 10 + 8 = 18$.<br/>The absolute minimum value is 18.</p>",
