    "chapter": "Probability",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We are given $P(A \\cup B) = 0.6$ and $P(A \\cap B) = 0.2$.<br/>We know $P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A \\cap B)$.<br/>So, $0.6 = P(A) + P(B) - 0.2 \\implies P(A) + P(B) = 0.8$.<br/>We want to find $P(\\overline{A}) + P(\\overline{B})$.<br/>$P(\\overline{A}) + P(\\overline{B}) = (1 - P(A)) + (1 - P(B)) = 2 - (P(A) + P(B)) = 2 - 0.8 = 1.2$.</p>",
