    "correct": "d",
    "chapter": "Probability",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the number of heads be $X$. $X \\sim \\text{Binomial}(100, p)$.<br/>Given $P(X = 50) = P(X = 51)$.<br/>$\\binom{100}{50} p^{50} (1-p)^{50} = \\binom{100}{51} p^{51} (1-p)^{49}$.<br/>Divide both sides by $p^{50} (1-p)^{49}$: $\\binom{100}{50} (1-p) = \\binom{100}{51} p$.<br/>$\\frac{100!}{50! 50!} (1-p) = \\frac{100!}{51! 49!} p$.<br/>Multiply by $\\frac{51! 50!}{100!}$: $51 (1-p) = 50 p$.<br/>$51 - 51p = 50p \\implies 101p = 51 \\implies p = \\frac{51}{101}$.</p>",
