    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the outcomes of the 4 rolls be $X_1, X_2, X_3, X_4$.<br/>Condition 1: Minimum face value $\\ge 2$.<br/>Condition 2: Maximum face value $\\le 5$.<br/>Both conditions are satisfied if and only if every roll results in a value in the set $\\{2, 3, 4, 5\\}$.<br/>However, this just means all values are from $\\{2,3,4,5\\}$, but the minimum must actually *be* $\\ge 2$ (which it is) and the maximum must actually *be* $\\le 5$ (which it is).<br/>The problem says \"minimum is not less than 2 and maximum is not greater than 5\". This implies $2 \\le X_i \\le 5$ for all $i$.<br/>The number of possible outcomes for a single roll is 6.<br/>The number of valid outcomes for a single roll is 4 (2, 3, 4, 5).<br/>Probability for one roll is $4/6 = 2/3$.<br/>Since there are 4 independent rolls, the required probability is $(2/3)^4 = 16/81$.</p>",
