    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>$A, B, C$ are mutually independent. This means $P(A \\cap B) = P(A)P(B)$, $P(B \\cap C) = P(B)P(C)$, $P(A \\cap C) = P(A)P(C)$, and $P(A \\cap B \\cap C) = P(A)P(B)P(C)$.<br/>For $S_1$: Check if $A$ and $B \\cup C$ are independent.<br/>$P(A \\cap (B \\cup C)) = P((A \\cap B) \\cup (A \\cap C)) = P(A \\cap B) + P(A \\cap C) - P(A \\cap B \\cap C)$<br/>$= P(A)P(B) + P(A)P(C) - P(A)P(B)P(C) = P(A) [P(B) + P(C) - P(B \\cap C)] = P(A) P(B \\cup C)$.<br/>Thus, $S_1$ is true.<br/>For $S_2$: Check if $A$ and $B \\cap C$ are independent.<br/>$P(A \\cap (B \\cap C)) = P(A \\cap B \\cap C) = P(A)P(B)P(C) = P(A)P(B \\cap C)$.<br/>Thus, $S_2$ is true.<br/>Both $S_1$ and $S_2$ are true.</p>",
