    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the probabilities of solving the problem be $P(A) = 1/2, P(B) = 3/4, P(C) = 1/4, P(D) = 1/8$.<br/>The probability that a person fails to solve is $1 - P(X)$.<br/>$P(A') = 1/2, P(B') = 1/4, P(C') = 3/4, P(D') = 7/8$.<br/>Since they work independently, the probability that ALL of them fail is the product of their failure probabilities:<br/>$P(\\text{All fail}) = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{7}{8} = \\frac{21}{256}$.<br/>The probability that at least one of them solves it correctly is $1 - P(\\text{All fail})$.<br/>$P(\\text{At least one}) = 1 - \\frac{21}{256} = \\frac{235}{256}$.</p>",
