    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>We are looking for non-negative integer solutions to $x + y + z = 10$.<br/>Total number of solutions is $\\binom{10 + 3 - 1}{3 - 1} = \\binom{12}{2} = 66$.<br/>We need the probability that $z$ is even. Let $z = 2k$, where $k \\in \\{0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}$.<br/>Then $x + y = 10 - 2k$. The number of solutions for a fixed $k$ is $(10 - 2k) + 1 = 11 - 2k$.<br/>Summing over all possible values of $k$:<br/>$k=0: 11$<br/>$k=1: 9$<br/>$k=2: 7$<br/>$k=3: 5$<br/>$k=4: 3$<br/>$k=5: 1$<br/>Total favorable solutions = $11 + 9 + 7 + 5 + 3 + 1 = 36$.<br/>Probability = $36 / 66 = 6 / 11$.</p>",
