    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>For $C_1$, $P(H) = 2/3$. Tossed twice, $\\alpha \\in \\{0, 1, 2\\}$.<br/>$P(\\alpha = 0) = (1/3)^2 = 1/9$<br/>$P(\\alpha = 1) = 2(2/3)(1/3) = 4/9$<br/>$P(\\alpha = 2) = (2/3)^2 = 4/9$<br/>For $C_2$, $P(H) = 1/3$. Tossed twice, $\\beta \\in \\{0, 1, 2\\}$.<br/>$P(\\beta = 0) = (2/3)^2 = 4/9$<br/>$P(\\beta = 1) = 2(1/3)(2/3) = 4/9$<br/>$P(\\beta = 2) = (1/3)^2 = 1/9$<br/>The roots of $x^2 - \\alpha x + \\beta = 0$ are real and equal if the discriminant is 0, so $\\alpha^2 - 4\\beta = 0 \\implies \\alpha^2 = 4\\beta$.<br/>Possible pairs for $(\\alpha, \\beta)$ from $\\{0,1,2\\}$ are:<br/>If $\\beta = 0$, $\\alpha = 0$. Pair: $(0,0)$.<br/>If $\\beta = 1$, $\\alpha = 2$. Pair: $(2,1)$.<br/>If $\\beta = 2$, $\\alpha^2 = 8$ (no integer solution).<br/>Probability = $P(\\alpha=0)P(\\beta=0) + P(\\alpha=2)P(\\beta=1)$<br/>$= (1/9)(4/9) + (4/9)(4/9) = 4/81 + 16/81 = 20/81$.</p>",
