    "text": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two events such that $P(X∣Y)= \\frac{1}{2}$ , $P(Y∣X)= \\frac{1}{3}$ and $P(X\\cap Y)= \\frac{1}{6}$ . Which of the following is(are) correct?",
