    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a, b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $P(X|Y) = 1/2 \\implies \\frac{P(X \\cap Y)}{P(Y)} = 1/2 \\implies \\frac{1/6}{P(Y)} = 1/2 \\implies P(Y) = 1/3$.<br/>Given $P(Y|X) = 1/3 \\implies \\frac{P(X \\cap Y)}{P(X)} = 1/3 \\implies \\frac{1/6}{P(X)} = 1/3 \\implies P(X) = 1/2$.<br/>Using these values, evaluate the options involving unions and complements.<br/>Options a and b are correct.</p>",
