    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_{10}$ be in A.P. with $a_1 = 2$ and $a_{10} = 3$.<br/>$a_1 + 9d = 3 \\implies 2 + 9d = 3 \\implies 9d = 1 \\implies d = 1/9$.<br/>$a_4 = a_1 + 3d = 2 + 3(1/9) = 2 + 1/3 = 7/3$.<br/>Let $h_1, h_2, \\dots, h_{10}$ be in H.P. with $h_1 = 2$ and $h_{10} = 3$.<br/>So $1/h_1, \\dots, 1/h_{10}$ are in A.P. with first term $1/2$ and 10th term $1/3$.<br/>$1/2 + 9D = 1/3 \\implies 9D = 1/3 - 1/2 = -1/6 \\implies D = -1/54$.<br/>$1/h_7 = 1/h_1 + 6D = 1/2 + 6(-1/54) = 1/2 - 1/9 = 7/18$.<br/>So $h_7 = 18/7$.<br/>$a_4 h_7 = (7/3) \\times (18/7) = 18/3 = 6$. Option d.</p>",
