    "chapter": "Sequences And Series",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the roots be $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. The harmonic mean (H.M.) of roots is $\\frac{2\\alpha\\beta}{\\alpha + \\beta}$.<br/>For $Ax^2 + Bx + C = 0$, $\\alpha + \\beta = -B/A$ and $\\alpha\\beta = C/A$.<br/>Thus H.M. = $\\frac{2(C/A)}{-B/A} = \\frac{2C}{-B}$.<br/>Here, $C = 8 + 2\\sqrt{5} = 2(4 + \\sqrt{5})$ and $-B = 4 + \\sqrt{5}$.<br/>H.M. = $\\frac{2 \\times 2(4+\\sqrt{5})}{4+\\sqrt{5}} = 4$. Option b.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Easy"
