    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Sum of infinite G.P. is $S = \\frac{a}{1 - r} = 4 \\implies a = 4(1 - r)$.<br/>Second term is $ar = 3/4$.<br/>Substitute $a$: $4(1 - r)r = 3/4 \\implies 16r(1 - r) = 3 \\implies 16r^2 - 16r + 3 = 0$.<br/>$(4r - 1)(4r - 3) = 0 \\implies r = 1/4$ or $r = 3/4$.<br/>If $r = 1/4$, $a = 4(1 - 1/4) = 3$. This gives $(3, 1/4)$.<br/>If $r = 3/4$, $a = 4(1 - 3/4) = 1$. This gives $(1, 3/4)$, which is not in the options.<br/>So $(a=3, r=1/4)$ matches option d.</p>",
