    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>The number of triangles formed by $n$ vertices is $T_n = \\binom{n}{3}$.<br/>$T_{n+1} - T_n = \\binom{n+1}{3} - \\binom{n}{3}$.<br/>Using Pascal's identity $\\binom{n+1}{k} = \\binom{n}{k} + \\binom{n}{k-1}$, we have $T_{n+1} - T_n = \\binom{n}{2}$.<br/>We are given $\\binom{n}{2} = 21 \\implies \\frac{n(n-1)}{2} = 21 \\implies n(n-1) = 42$.<br/>The positive integer solution is $n = 7$. Option b.</p>",
