    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $a, b, c, d$ are in A.P.<br/>Divide each term by the product $abcd$.<br/>The resulting sequence is $\\frac{a}{abcd}, \\frac{b}{abcd}, \\frac{c}{abcd}, \\frac{d}{abcd}$, which simplifies to $\\frac{1}{bcd}, \\frac{1}{acd}, \\frac{1}{abd}, \\frac{1}{abc}$.<br/>Since dividing an A.P. by a non-zero constant gives an A.P., the sequence $\\frac{1}{bcd}, \\frac{1}{acd}, \\frac{1}{abd}, \\frac{1}{abc}$ is in A.P.<br/>Therefore, their reciprocals $bcd, acd, abd, abc$ are in Harmonic Progression (H.P.).<br/>Reversing the order, $abc, abd, acd, bcd$ are also in H.P. Option d.</p>",
