    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: n = 11</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>First A.P.: $2, 5, 8, \\dots$ ($a=2, d=3$). Sum of $2n$ terms is $S_{2n} = \\frac{2n}{2} [2(2) + (2n-1)3] = n[4 + 6n - 3] = n(6n + 1)$.<br/>Second A.P.: $57, 59, 61, \\dots$ ($A=57, D=2$). Sum of $n$ terms is $S_n = \\frac{n}{2} [2(57) + (n-1)2] = \\frac{n}{2} [114 + 2n - 2] = n(n + 56)$.<br/>Equating them: $n(6n + 1) = n(n + 56)$.<br/>Since $n \\neq 0$, divide by $n$: $6n + 1 = n + 56 \\implies 5n = 55 \\implies n = 11$.</p>",
