    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the sum be $S = a_1 + a_2 + \\dots + a_{n-1} + 2a_n$.<br/>This is a sum of $n$ positive terms. By AM-GM inequality:<br/>$\\frac{a_1 + a_2 + \\dots + a_{n-1} + 2a_n}{n} \\ge (a_1 a_2 \\dots a_{n-1} (2a_n))^{1/n}$.<br/>We know $a_1 a_2 \\dots a_n = c$.<br/>So the RHS is $(2c)^{1/n}$.<br/>Thus, $S \\ge n(2c)^{1/n}$. The minimum value is $n(2c)^{1/n}$. Option a.</p>",
