    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $a, b, c$ are in A.P., so $b = \\frac{a+c}{2}$. Also $a+b+c = 3/2 \\implies 3b = 3/2 \\implies b = 1/2$.<br/>Let $a = 1/2 - d$ and $c = 1/2 + d$. Since $a < b < c$, $d > 0$.<br/>Given $a^2, b^2, c^2$ are in G.P. $\\implies (b^2)^2 = a^2 c^2 \\implies b^4 = (ac)^2$.<br/>So $(1/2)^4 = ((1/2 - d)(1/2 + d))^2 = (1/4 - d^2)^2$.<br/>$1/16 = (1/4 - d^2)^2 \\implies 1/4 - d^2 = \\pm 1/4$.<br/>If $1/4 - d^2 = 1/4 \\implies d^2 = 0$, but $d > 0$.<br/>If $1/4 - d^2 = -1/4 \\implies d^2 = 1/2 \\implies d = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$.<br/>Then $a = 1/2 - 1/\\sqrt{2}$. Option d.</p>",
