    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Sum of infinite G.P. is $S = \\frac{x}{1-r} = 5$.<br/>We know for an infinite G.P. to converge, $-1 < r < 1$.<br/>From the sum, $1 - r = x/5 \\implies r = 1 - x/5$.<br/>Substitute $r$ into the inequality: $-1 < 1 - x/5 < 1$.<br/>Subtract 1: $-2 < -x/5 < 0$.<br/>Multiply by $-5$: $10 > x > 0 \\implies 0 < x < 10$. Option c.</p>",
