    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $S_1 = \\alpha + \\beta = -b/a$, $S_2 = \\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = S_1^2 - 2\\alpha\\beta = b^2/a^2 - 2c/a = \\frac{b^2 - 2ac}{a^2}$.<br/>$S_3 = \\alpha^3 + \\beta^3 = S_1(S_2 - \\alpha\\beta) = (-b/a)(\\frac{b^2 - 2ac}{a^2} - \\frac{c}{a}) = \\frac{-b(b^2 - 3ac)}{a^3}$.<br/>Given $S_1, S_2, S_3$ are in G.P. $\\implies S_2^2 = S_1 S_3$.<br/>$\\left( \\frac{b^2 - 2ac}{a^2} \\right)^2 = \\left( \\frac{-b}{a} \\right) \\left( \\frac{-b(b^2 - 3ac)}{a^3} \\right)$.<br/>$\\frac{(b^2 - 2ac)^2}{a^4} = \\frac{b^2(b^2 - 3ac)}{a^4}$.<br/>$b^4 - 4ab^2c + 4a^2c^2 = b^4 - 3ab^2c$.<br/>$4a^2c^2 - ab^2c = 0 \\implies ac(4ac - b^2) = 0$.<br/>Since $\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac$, this is $ac(-\\Delta) = 0 \\implies ac\\Delta = 0$.<br/>Assuming $a \\neq 0$, we have $c\\Delta = 0$. Option a.</p>",
