    "text": "The sum of the squares of three distinct real numbers, which are in G.P. is ${s}^{2}$ . If their sum is $\\alpha s$ , show that ${\\alpha }^{2}\\in \\left( \\frac{1}{3} ,1 \\right) \\cup (1,3]$",
