    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: \\frac{n(2n+1)(4n+1)-3}{3}</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Sum of infinite G.P. $S = a / (1 - r)$.<br/>For $S_k$, first term is $k$, common ratio is $\\frac{1}{k+1}$.<br/>$S_k = \\frac{k}{1 - \\frac{1}{k+1}} = \\frac{k}{\\frac{k}{k+1}} = k+1$.<br/>So $S_k = k+1$.<br/>We need to find $S_1^2 + S_2^2 + \\dots + S_{2n-1}^2$.<br/>This is $2^2 + 3^2 + \\dots + (2n)^2$.<br/>$= \\sum_{k=1}^{2n} k^2 - 1^2 = \\frac{(2n)(2n+1)(4n+1)}{6} - 1$.<br/>$= \\frac{n(2n+1)(4n+1)}{3} - 1 = \\frac{n(2n+1)(4n+1) - 3}{3}$.</p>",
