    "correct": "3050",
    "chapter": "Sequences And Series",
    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 3050</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Sum of integers from 1 to 100 divisible by 2: $S_2 = 2 + 4 + \\dots + 100$. This is an A.P. with 50 terms. $S_2 = \\frac{50}{2}(2 + 100) = 25 \\times 102 = 2550$.<br/>Sum of integers from 1 to 100 divisible by 5: $S_5 = 5 + 10 + \\dots + 100$. This is an A.P. with 20 terms. $S_5 = \\frac{20}{2}(5 + 100) = 10 \\times 105 = 1050$.<br/>Sum of integers from 1 to 100 divisible by both 2 and 5 (i.e., 10): $S_{10} = 10 + 20 + \\dots + 100$. This is an A.P. with 10 terms. $S_{10} = \\frac{10}{2}(10 + 100) = 5 \\times 110 = 550$.<br/>By principle of inclusion-exclusion, the sum of integers divisible by 2 or 5 is $S = S_2 + S_5 - S_{10}$.<br/>$S = 2550 + 1050 - 550 = 3600 - 550 = 3050$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Medium"
