    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 1:4 \\text{ or } 4:1</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the numbers be $a$ and $b$.<br/>H.M. = $\\frac{2ab}{a+b}$, G.M. = $\\sqrt{ab}$.<br/>Given $\\frac{\\text{H.M.}}{\\text{G.M.}} = \\frac{4}{5} \\implies \\frac{\\frac{2ab}{a+b}}{\\sqrt{ab}} = \\frac{4}{5}$.<br/>$\\frac{2\\sqrt{ab}}{a+b} = \\frac{4}{5} \\implies \\frac{\\sqrt{ab}}{a+b} = \\frac{2}{5}$.<br/>Let $a/b = k$. Divide numerator and denominator by $b$: $\\frac{\\sqrt{k}}{k+1} = \\frac{2}{5}$.<br/>$5\\sqrt{k} = 2(k+1) \\implies 25k = 4(k^2 + 2k + 1) = 4k^2 + 8k + 4$.<br/>$4k^2 - 17k + 4 = 0 \\implies (4k - 1)(k - 4) = 0$.<br/>$k = 1/4$ or $k = 4$.<br/>So $a:b = 1:4$ or $4:1$.</p>",
