    "text": "Let $p$ and $q$ be roots of the equation ${x}^{2}-2x+A=0$ and let $r$ and $s$ be the roots of the equation ${x}^{2}-18x+B=0$ . If $p<q<r<s$ are in arithmetic progression, then $A=…$ . and $B=$ $$",
