    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: -3, 77</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>$p, q$ are roots of $x^2 - 2x + A = 0 \\implies p+q = 2$ and $pq = A$.<br/>$r, s$ are roots of $x^2 - 18x + B = 0 \\implies r+s = 18$ and $rs = B$.<br/>$p, q, r, s$ are in A.P.<br/>Let $p = a - 3d, q = a - d, r = a + d, s = a + 3d$.<br/>$p+q = 2a - 4d = 2 \\implies a - 2d = 1$.<br/>$r+s = 2a + 4d = 18 \\implies a + 2d = 9$.<br/>Adding them: $2a = 10 \\implies a = 5$.<br/>Then $5 + 2d = 9 \\implies 2d = 4 \\implies d = 2$.<br/>So the roots are:<br/>$p = 5 - 6 = -1$<br/>$q = 5 - 2 = 3$<br/>$r = 5 + 2 = 7$<br/>$s = 5 + 6 = 11$<br/>$A = pq = (-1)(3) = -3$.<br/>$B = rs = (7)(11) = 77$.</p>",
