    "text": "Let $\\vec{75⋯57}$ denote the $(r+2)$ digit number where the first and the last digits are 7 and the remaining $r$ digits are 5. Consider the sum $=77+757+7557+$ $….+ \\vec{75⋯57} 98$ . If $S= \\vec{\\frac{75⋯57}{n} +m} 99$ , where $m$ and $n$ are natural numbers less than 3000 , then the value of $m+n$ is",
