    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>In $\\Delta PQR$, $R = 90^\\circ \\implies P + Q = 90^\\circ \\implies \\frac{P+Q}{2} = 45^\\circ$.<br/>$\\tan\\left(\\frac{P+Q}{2}\\right) = \\tan 45^\\circ = 1$.<br/>$\\frac{\\tan(P/2) + \\tan(Q/2)}{1 - \\tan(P/2)\\tan(Q/2)} = 1$.<br/>We know $\\tan(P/2)$ and $\\tan(Q/2)$ are roots of $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$.<br/>Sum of roots = $-b/a$. Product of roots = $c/a$.<br/>So $\\frac{-b/a}{1 - c/a} = 1 \\implies \\frac{-b}{a - c} = 1 \\implies -b = a - c \\implies c = a + b$.<br/>Option a correctly represents this relation.</p>",
