    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $\\alpha + \\beta = \\pi/2$ and $\\alpha - \\beta = \\gamma$ (from $\\beta + \\gamma = \\alpha$).<br/>We want to find $\\tan \\alpha$.<br/>From $\\alpha - \\beta = \\gamma$, take $\\tan$ on both sides: $\\tan(\\alpha - \\beta) = \\tan \\gamma$.<br/>$\\frac{\\tan \\alpha - \\tan \\beta}{1 + \\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta} = \\tan \\gamma$.<br/>Since $\\alpha + \\beta = \\pi/2$, $\\tan \\beta = \\cot \\alpha = 1/\\tan \\alpha$.<br/>So $\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta = 1$.<br/>The denominator becomes $1 + 1 = 2$.<br/>$\\frac{\\tan \\alpha - \\tan \\beta}{2} = \\tan \\gamma \\implies \\tan \\alpha - \\tan \\beta = 2 \\tan \\gamma$.<br/>$\\tan \\alpha = \\tan \\beta + 2 \\tan \\gamma$. Option c.</p>",
