    "chapter": "Trigonometric Equations",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>For $7\\cos x + 5\\sin x = 2k + 1$ to have a solution, the RHS must be within the range of the LHS.<br/>The maximum value of $7\\cos x + 5\\sin x$ is $\\sqrt{7^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{49 + 25} = \\sqrt{74} \\approx 8.6$.<br/>The minimum value is $-\\sqrt{74} \\approx -8.6$.<br/>So $-\\sqrt{74} \\le 2k + 1 \\le \\sqrt{74}$.<br/>$-8.6 \\le 2k + 1 \\le 8.6 \\implies -9.6 \\le 2k \\le 7.6 \\implies -4.8 \\le k \\le 3.8$.<br/>The integral values of $k$ are $-4, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3$.<br/>There are 8 integral values. Option b.</p>",
