    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>$\\sqrt{3}\\sec x + \\csc x + 2(\\tan x - \\cot x) = 0$.<br/>Multiply by $\\sin x \\cos x$:<br/>$\\sqrt{3}\\sin x + \\cos x + 2(\\sin^2 x - \\cos^2 x) = 0$.<br/>$2(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x + \\frac{1}{2}\\cos x) - 2\\cos 2x = 0$.<br/>$\\sin(x + \\pi/6) = \\cos 2x$.<br/>$\\cos(\\pi/2 - (x + \\pi/6)) = \\cos 2x \\implies \\cos(\\pi/3 - x) = \\cos 2x$.<br/>$2x = 2n\\pi \\pm (\\pi/3 - x)$.<br/>Case 1: $2x = 2n\\pi + \\pi/3 - x \\implies 3x = 2n\\pi + \\pi/3 \\implies x = 2n\\pi/3 + \\pi/9$.<br/>In $(-\\pi, \\pi)$, for $n=0, x=\\pi/9$. For $n=1, x = 7\\pi/9$. For $n=-1, x = -5\\pi/9$.<br/>Case 2: $2x = 2n\\pi - \\pi/3 + x \\implies x = 2n\\pi - \\pi/3$.<br/>In $(-\\pi, \\pi)$, for $n=0, x=-\\pi/3$.<br/>Check constraints: $x \\neq 0, \\pm\\pi/2$. All found solutions are valid.<br/>Sum = $\\pi/9 + 7\\pi/9 - 5\\pi/9 - \\pi/3 = 3\\pi/9 - \\pi/3 = \\pi/3 - \\pi/3 = 0$. Option c.</p>",
