    "id": "jee_adv_math_trigonometric_equations_33",
    "number": "33",
    "type": "single mcq",
    "text": "Prove that for any positive integer $k$ , $\\frac{sin2kx}{sinx} =2[cosx+cos3x+cos5x+…+cos(2k-1)x]$ Hence prove that ${∫}_{0}^{\\pi /2} sin2kx⋅cotx⋅dx= \\frac{\\pi }{2}$",
