    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 30^\\circ</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>$\\tan(x+100^\\circ) = \\tan(x+50^\\circ) \\tan x \\tan(x-50^\\circ)$.<br/>We know $\\tan(A)\\tan(60^\\circ-A)\\tan(60^\\circ+A) = \\tan 3A$.<br/>This identity can be related or the equation can be converted into sine/cosine to solve for $x$.<br/>By systematically solving the trigonometric equation, the smallest positive $x$ is found to be $30^\\circ$.</p>",
