    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: F</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>$\\sin^4\\theta - 2\\sin^2\\theta - 1 = 0$.<br/>Let $u = \\sin^2\\theta$. $u^2 - 2u - 1 = 0 \\implies u = \\frac{2 \\pm \\sqrt{4 + 4}}{2} = 1 \\pm \\sqrt{2}$.<br/>Since $0 \\le u \\le 1$, $u = 1 - \\sqrt{2} \\approx -0.414$ is rejected.<br/>$u = 1 + \\sqrt{2} \\approx 2.414$ is rejected.<br/>There is no real solution for $u$ in $[0, 1]$.<br/>Thus, there is no solution for $\\theta$. The statement is False.</p>",
