    "chapter": "Trigonometric Equations",
    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: \\cos (\\log \\theta)</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $\\theta \\in (e^{-\\pi/2}, \\pi/2)$. We want to compare $\\cos(\\log\\theta)$ and $\\log(\\cos\\theta)$.<br/>For $\\theta \\in (0, \\pi/2)$, $\\cos\\theta < 1$, so $\\log(\\cos\\theta) < 0$.<br/>Also, $\\theta > e^{-\\pi/2} \\implies \\log\\theta > -\\pi/2$.<br/>And $\\theta < \\pi/2 \\approx 1.57 < e^{\\pi/2} \\approx 4.81$, so $\\log\\theta < \\pi/2$.<br/>Thus $\\log\\theta \\in (-\\pi/2, \\pi/2)$.<br/>In this interval, the cosine function is positive, so $\\cos(\\log\\theta) > 0$.<br/>Therefore, $\\cos(\\log\\theta) > 0 > \\log(\\cos\\theta)$.<br/>The larger is $\\cos(\\log\\theta)$.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
