    "correct": "b",
    "chapter": "Trigonometric Equations",
    "topic": "Match The Following",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>(I) $\\cos x + \\sin x = 1 \\implies \\cos(x - \\pi/4) = 1/\\sqrt{2}$. Solutions in $(-2\\pi/3, 2\\pi/3)$: $x=0, \\pi/2$. (2 elements $\\rightarrow$ P).<br/>(II) $\\sqrt{3}\\tan 3x = 1 \\implies \\tan 3x = 1/\\sqrt{3} \\implies 3x = n\\pi + \\pi/6$. Solutions in $(-5\\pi/18, 5\\pi/18)$: $x = \\pi/18, -5\\pi/18$ (not inclusive). Thus $3x \\in (-5\\pi/6, 5\\pi/6)$. Solutions: $\\pi/6, \\pi/6 - \\pi = -5\\pi/6$. Wait, $-5\\pi/6$ is open bound. So 2 solutions $\\rightarrow$ P.<br/>(III) $2\\cos 2x = \\sqrt{3} \\implies \\cos 2x = \\sqrt{3}/2$. $2x \\in (-12\\pi/5, 12\\pi/5)$. $2x = \\pm\\pi/6, \\pm\\pi/6 \\pm 2\\pi$. This gives 6 elements $\\rightarrow$ T.<br/>(IV) $\\sin x - \\cos x = 1 \\implies \\sin(x - \\pi/4) = 1/\\sqrt{2}$. Solutions in $(-7\\pi/4, 7\\pi/4)$: $x = \\pi/2, \\pi, \\dots$ gives 4 elements $\\rightarrow$ R.<br/>Match is (I) $\\rightarrow$ P, (II) $\\rightarrow$ P, (III) $\\rightarrow$ T, (IV) $\\rightarrow$ R. Option b.</p>",
