    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: d</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>$\\cos(\\alpha - \\beta) = 1 \\implies \\alpha - \\beta = 2n\\pi$.<br/>Since $\\alpha, \\beta \\in [-\\pi, \\pi]$, the only possible difference is 0 or $\\pm 2\\pi$.<br/>If $\\alpha = \\beta$, then $\\cos(\\alpha + \\alpha) = 1/e \\implies \\cos 2\\alpha = 1/e$.<br/>$2\\alpha = \\pm \\arccos(1/e) + 2k\\pi$.<br/>$\\alpha = \\pm \\frac{1}{2}\\arccos(1/e) + k\\pi$.<br/>These values give valid pairs of $(\\alpha, \\beta)$.<br/>Option d represents these specific solutions.</p>",
