    "chapter": "Trigonometric Ratios And Identities",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the radius of each coin be $r = 1$.<br/>The distance between the centers of the coins is $2r = 2$.<br/>The triangle formed by the centers of the 3 coins is equilateral with side length $a = 2$.<br/>The distance from a vertex of the large triangle to the center of the nearest coin is $r/\\tan 30^\\circ = 1 / (1/\\sqrt{3}) = \\sqrt{3}$.<br/>The side length of the large equilateral triangle is $2r + 2 \\sqrt{3} = 2 + 2\\sqrt{3}$.<br/>Area $= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} (side)^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} (2 + 2\\sqrt{3})^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} 4(1 + \\sqrt{3})^2 = \\sqrt{3}(1 + 3 + 2\\sqrt{3}) = \\sqrt{3}(4 + 2\\sqrt{3}) = 4\\sqrt{3} + 6$.<br/>Option b perfectly matches this value.</p>",
