    "chapter": "Trigonometric Ratios And Identities",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>For $\\theta \\in (0, \\pi/4)$, $\\tan\\theta \\in (0, 1)$ and $\\cot\\theta \\in (1, \\infty)$.<br/>Let $x = \\tan\\theta$. Then $0 < x < 1$ and $\\cot\\theta = 1/x > 1$.<br/>$t_1 = x^x$, $t_2 = x^{1/x}$, $t_3 = (1/x)^x = x^{-x}$, $t_4 = (1/x)^{1/x} = x^{-1/x}$.<br/>Since $0 < x < 1$, $x^{-1/x} > x^{-x} > 1$, and $x^x > x^{1/x}$ since $x < 1/x$ and base $x < 1$.<br/>So $t_4 > t_3 > t_1 > t_2$.<br/>This ordering corresponds to option b.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
