    "number": "19",
    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "Let $\\frac{\\pi }{2} <x<\\pi$ be such that $cotx= \\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{11}}$ . Then $\\left( sin \\frac{11x}{2} \\right) (sin6x-cos6x)+ \\left( cos \\frac{11x}{2} \\right) (sin6x+cos6x)$ is equal to",
    "images": [],
