    "chapter": "Trigonometric Ratios And Identities",
    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: 6</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>$\\sin^3 x \\sin 3x = (\\frac{3\\sin x - \\sin 3x}{4}) \\sin 3x = \\frac{3}{4}\\sin x \\sin 3x - \\frac{1}{4}\\sin^2 3x$.<br/>$= \\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} (\\cos 2x - \\cos 4x) - \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} (1 - \\cos 6x)$.<br/>$= -\\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{3}{8}\\cos 2x - \\frac{3}{8}\\cos 4x + \\frac{1}{8}\\cos 6x$.<br/>This matches the form $\\sum_{m=0}^n C_m \\cos mx$.<br/>The highest multiple of $x$ is $6x$, so $n=6$.</p>",
