    "chapter": "Trigonometric Ratios And Identities",
    "topic": "Fill In The Blanks",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: \\frac{1}{64}</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $P = \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{14} \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{14} \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{14} \\sin \\frac{7\\pi}{14} \\sin \\frac{9\\pi}{14} \\sin \\frac{11\\pi}{14} \\sin \\frac{13\\pi}{14}$.<br/>Since $\\sin(\\pi - x) = \\sin x$, we have:<br/>$\\sin \\frac{13\\pi}{14} = \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{14}$<br/>$\\sin \\frac{11\\pi}{14} = \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{14}$<br/>$\\sin \\frac{9\\pi}{14} = \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{14}$<br/>$\\sin \\frac{7\\pi}{14} = \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{2} = 1$.<br/>So $P = ( \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{14} \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{14} \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{14} )^2$.<br/>Now let $Q = \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{14} \\cos \\frac{3\\pi}{14} \\cos \\frac{5\\pi}{14}$.<br/>$\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{14} = \\cos(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{14}) = \\cos \\frac{6\\pi}{14} = \\cos \\frac{3\\pi}{7}$.<br/>Similarly $\\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{14} = \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{14} = \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7}$ and $\\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{14} = \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{14} = \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{7}$.<br/>So $\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{14} \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{14} \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{14} = \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{3\\pi}{7}$.<br/>Also $\\cos \\frac{3\\pi}{7} = -\\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7}$.<br/>The product $\\cos \\frac{\\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{4\\pi}{7} = -1/8$.<br/>So $\\cos \\frac{\\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{2\\pi}{7} \\cos \\frac{3\\pi}{7} = 1/8$.<br/>$P = (1/8)^2 = 1/64$.</p>",
