    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>$\\vec{a} = 2\\hat{i} + \\hat{j} - 2\\hat{k}$, so $|\\vec{a}| = \\sqrt{4+1+4} = 3$.<br/>$\\vec{b} = \\hat{i} + \\hat{j}$.<br/>$\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\end{vmatrix} = \\hat{i}(2) - \\hat{j}(2) + \\hat{k}(2 - 1) = 2\\hat{i} - 2\\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$.<br/>$|\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b}| = \\sqrt{4+4+1} = 3$.<br/>Given $|\\vec{c} - \\vec{a}| = 2\\sqrt{2} \\implies |\\vec{c}|^2 + |\\vec{a}|^2 - 2\\vec{c}\\cdot\\vec{a} = 8$.<br/>Since $\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{c} = |\\vec{c}|$, we have $|\\vec{c}|^2 + 9 - 2|\\vec{c}| = 8 \\implies |\\vec{c}|^2 - 2|\\vec{c}| + 1 = 0 \\implies (|\\vec{c}| - 1)^2 = 0 \\implies |\\vec{c}| = 1$.<br/>We want $|(\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b}) \\times \\vec{c}| = |\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b}| |\\vec{c}| \\sin 30^\\circ = (3)(1)(1/2) = 3/2$. Option b.</p>",
