    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let $\\vec{c} = x\\vec{a} + y\\vec{b}$. (since they are coplanar).<br/>Actually, since $\\vec{c}$ is coplanar with $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$, and perpendicular to $\\vec{a}$, $\\vec{c}$ is parallel to $\\vec{a} \\times (\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b})$.<br/>Wait, $\\vec{a} \\times (\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b}) = (\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b})\\vec{a} - (\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{a})\\vec{b}$.<br/>$\\vec{a} = 2\\hat{i} + \\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$. $|\\vec{a}|^2 = 4+1+1 = 6$.<br/>$\\vec{b} = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} - \\hat{k}$.<br/>$\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} = 2(1) + 1(2) + 1(-1) = 3$.<br/>Vector perpendicular to $\\vec{a}$ in the plane of $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}$ is $\\vec{v} = \\vec{b} - \\frac{\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}}{|\\vec{a}|^2}\\vec{a} = \\vec{b} - \\frac{3}{6}\\vec{a} = \\vec{b} - \\frac{1}{2}\\vec{a}$.<br/>$\\vec{v} = (\\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} - \\hat{k}) - \\frac{1}{2}(2\\hat{i} + \\hat{j} + \\hat{k}) = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} - \\hat{k} - \\hat{i} - \\frac{1}{2}\\hat{j} - \\frac{1}{2}\\hat{k} = \\frac{3}{2}\\hat{j} - \\frac{3}{2}\\hat{k}$.<br/>Unit vector $\\vec{c} = \\pm \\frac{\\frac{3}{2}(\\hat{j} - \\hat{k})}{\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{2}} = \\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\hat{j} - \\hat{k})$.<br/>This is $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(-\\hat{j} + \\hat{k})$ or $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\hat{j} - \\hat{k})$.<br/>Option a gives $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(-\\hat{j} + \\hat{k})$.</p>",
