    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: b</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $\\vec{a} + \\vec{b} + \\vec{c} = \\vec{0}$ and they are unit vectors.<br/>Take dot product with $\\vec{a}$: $1 + \\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} + \\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{c} = 0$.<br/>Similarly, $\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} + \\vec{b}\\cdot\\vec{c} + \\vec{c}\\cdot\\vec{a} = -3/2$.<br/>This means the angle between any two of them is $120^\\circ$.<br/>Also $\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b} = \\vec{b} \\times \\vec{c} = \\vec{c} \\times \\vec{a}$.<br/>Option b correctly represents one of these symmetric relations.</p>",
