    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>$\\vec{OP} = \\vec{a}\\cos t + \\vec{b}\\sin t$.<br/>$|\\vec{OP}|^2 = |\\vec{a}|^2\\cos^2 t + |\\vec{b}|^2\\sin^2 t + 2(\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b})\\sin t \\cos t = 1 + (\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b})\\sin 2t$.<br/>Let $\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} = \\cos\\theta$. Since the angle is acute, $\\cos\\theta > 0$.<br/>$|\\vec{OP}|^2 = 1 + \\cos\\theta \\sin 2t$.<br/>Maximized when $\\sin 2t = 1 \\implies 2t = \\pi/2 \\implies t = \\pi/4$.<br/>At $t = \\pi/4$, $\\vec{OP} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vec{a} + \\vec{b})$.<br/>So $\\vec{u} = \\frac{\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}}{|\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}|}$ and $M = \\sqrt{1 + \\cos\\theta}$.<br/>Option a describes this relationship.</p>",
