    "number": "38",
    "type": "numerical",
    "text": "Let $\\vec{PR} =3 \\vec{i} + \\vec{j} -2 \\vec{k}$ and $\\vec{SQ} = \\vec{i} -3 \\vec{j} -4 \\vec{k}$ determine diagonals of a parallelogram $PQRS$ and $\\vec{PT} = \\vec{i} +2 \\vec{j} +3 \\vec{k}$ be another vector. Then the volume of the parallelopiped determined by the vectors $\\vec{PT} , \\vec{PQ}$ and $\\vec{PS}$ is",
    "images": [],
    "options": [],
    "correct": "10",
    "chapter": "Vectors",
    "topic": "Multiple Choice Questions (With One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Let the sides of the parallelogram be $\\vec{a} = \\vec{PQ}$ and $\\vec{b} = \\vec{PS}$.<br/>Diagonals are $\\vec{PR} = \\vec{a} + \\vec{b}$ and $\\vec{SQ} = \\vec{a} - \\vec{b}$.<br/>Given $\\vec{a} + \\vec{b} = 3\\hat{i} + \\hat{j} - 2\\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{a} - \\vec{b} = \\hat{i} - 3\\hat{j} - 4\\hat{k}$.<br/>Adding: $2\\vec{a} = 4\\hat{i} - 2\\hat{j} - 6\\hat{k} \\implies \\vec{a} = 2\\hat{i} - \\hat{j} - 3\\hat{k}$.<br/>Subtracting: $2\\vec{b} = 2\\hat{i} + 4\\hat{j} + 2\\hat{k} \\implies \\vec{b} = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$.<br/>We need the volume of parallelepiped with edges $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{PT}$.<br/>$\\vec{PT} = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + 3\\hat{k}$.<br/>Volume $= |[\\vec{PT} \\vec{a} \\vec{b}]| = \\left| \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} \\right|$.<br/>$= | 1(-1 + 6) - 2(2 - (-3)) + 3(4 - (-1)) | = | 1(5) - 2(5) + 3(5) | = | 5 - 10 + 15 | = 10$.<br/>Option c corresponds to 10.</p>",
    "needsManualReview": false,
    "difficulty": "Medium"
