    "type": "multiple mcq",
    "text": "Let $O$ be the origin and $\\vec{OA} =2 \\vec{i} +2 \\vec{j} + \\vec{k}$ , $\\vec{OB} = \\vec{i} -2 \\vec{j} +2 \\vec{k}$ and $\\vec{OC} = \\frac{1}{2} ( \\vec{OB} -\\lambda \\vec{OA} )$ for some $\\lambda >0$ . If $| \\vec{OB} \\times \\vec{OC} |= \\frac{9}{2}$ , then which of the following statements is (are) TRUE?",
    "images": [],
