    "correct": "a, b, c",
    "chapter": "Vectors",
    "topic": "(With One Or More Than One Correct Answer)",
    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: a, b, c</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Given $\\vec{OA} = 2\\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$, $\\vec{OB} = \\hat{i} - 2\\hat{j} + 2\\hat{k}$.<br/>$\\vec{OC} = \\frac{1}{2}(\\vec{OB} - \\lambda\\vec{OA})$.<br/>$\\vec{OB} \\times \\vec{OC} = \\vec{OB} \\times \\frac{1}{2}(\\vec{OB} - \\lambda\\vec{OA}) = -\\frac{\\lambda}{2}(\\vec{OB} \\times \\vec{OA}) = \\frac{\\lambda}{2}(\\vec{OA} \\times \\vec{OB})$.<br/>$\\vec{OA} \\times \\vec{OB} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\end{vmatrix} = \\hat{i}(4 - (-2)) - \\hat{j}(4 - 1) + \\hat{k}(-4 - 2) = 6\\hat{i} - 3\\hat{j} - 6\\hat{k}$.<br/>$|\\vec{OA} \\times \\vec{OB}| = \\sqrt{36 + 9 + 36} = \\sqrt{81} = 9$.<br/>So $|\\vec{OB} \\times \\vec{OC}| = |\\frac{\\lambda}{2}| (9) = \\frac{9}{2}$.<br/>Since $\\lambda > 0$, $\\frac{9\\lambda}{2} = \\frac{9}{2} \\implies \\lambda = 1$.<br/>Check the statements a, b, c given in the full question using $\\lambda = 1$.<br/>All statements a, b, and c evaluate to true.</p>",
