    "solution": "<p><strong>Ans: \\frac{-146}{17}</strong></p><p><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br/>Points A, B, C, D are coplanar.<br/>$\\vec{AB} = (-1)\\hat{i} + 5\\hat{j} - 3\\hat{k}$.<br/>$\\vec{AC} = -4\\hat{i} + 3\\hat{j} + 3\\hat{k}$.<br/>$\\vec{AD} = 1\\hat{i} + 7\\hat{j} + (\\lambda+1)\\hat{k}$.<br/>They are coplanar if $[\\vec{AB} \\vec{AC} \\vec{AD}] = 0$.<br/>$\\begin{vmatrix} -1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 7 & \\lambda+1 \\end{vmatrix} = 0$.<br/>$-1(3\\lambda + 3 - 21) - 5(-4\\lambda - 4 - 3) - 3(-28 - 3) = 0$.<br/>$-1(3\\lambda - 18) - 5(-4\\lambda - 7) - 3(-31) = 0$.<br/>$-3\\lambda + 18 + 20\\lambda + 35 + 93 = 0$.<br/>$17\\lambda + 146 = 0 \\implies 17\\lambda = -146 \\implies \\lambda = -146/17$.</p>",
